{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg --files docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness | rg 'self-reference|dependency-design'\nnl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/claude-r1.md\"","aggregated_output":"docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/codex-r1.stream\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/brief.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/claude-r1.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/codex-r1.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/selection_census.py\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/round2-brief.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/codex-r2.stream\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/codex-r2.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/selection-census.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/self-reference/reference_census.py\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/self-reference/RESULT.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/self-reference/reference-census.md\n     1\t# Claude's read, round 1 (written before reading codex-r1.md)\n     2\t\n     3\tScope: the product poc-v118 (no seeds). New facts gathered at $0 for this round:\n     4\t- `selection-census.md`: the matcher's \"part_of\" is undirected by its own criterion and noisy (old-2 seq 148: total revenue FY2027\n     5\t  \"part_of\" Data Center 0.99; old-1 seq 1410: FY2028 growth \"part_of\" FY2027 Data Center 0.79; aggregates \"part_of\" single deals).\n     6\t  It cannot choose an edge or its direction. The typed keys (`view_keys`: measure, scope, period) separate the pairs cleanly: in all\n     7\t  three draws a `segment_revenue` / `product_revenue` question and a `total_revenue` question of the same company and fiscal year.\n     8\t- Creation order differs: old-1 and old-3 open total revenue first (seq 22); **old-2 opens Data Center at seq 62 and total revenue at\n     9\t  seq 148**. A rule that only acts when the reader is created misses one draw in three.\n    10\t- **Filing:** in old-2, **106** evidence items are linked to both v9 (Data Center) and v14 (total). With D265 read literally on a\n    11\t  chosen edge, all 106 would leave total revenue. The Wall Street estimate items (e4061, e4097, e4348) are linked to v14 only (e4348\n    12\t  also to v17, v21, v35), so they stay either way.\n    13\t- Matching describes a question by its text and ladder only (`views/matching.py` `describe_view`, lines 161–170): a changed\n    14\t  judgement does not reach the matcher's requests. Not yet checked: whether the reading step's shown questions carry conclusions.\n    15\t- The self-made reference (`../self-reference/RESULT.md`) shares a cause: the market figure for the whole sits under the whole only,\n    16\t  and the part never reads it.\n    17\t\n    18\t## Per item\n    19\t1. **Who chooses and which way.** Recommend: code writes a component edge from the typed keys: same company, the same fiscal period,\n    20\t   one question's measure a segment or product revenue and the other's total revenue; the part reads the whole. This is identity\n    21\t   (an accounting fact on typed fields), not importance; the judge already holds \"a component cannot exceed its whole\"\n    22\t   (judging-v7 line 4 and 9). The edge is written at whichever question's creation completes the pair (D191 point 2's \"a dependency\n    23\t   may be added to an existing thesis by a later item\", Alex: \"可以\"). Direction: the part reads the whole, because the market's\n    24\t   figures (consensus, guidance) are company-wide and filed under the whole (D207); PRD 06 lines 131–132 and D537 agree, the probe\n    25\t   showed it works. D368 item 4 (root reads drivers) is about seed driver edges, a different relation (a driver is a judgement of\n    26\t   cause, not an identity); it is not built here. Departing from D51's chooser (the matching call) for this identity case is Alex's\n    27\t   choice. The direction label is computed from the two ladders (`matching.ladder_direction` and the bullish label of the part's\n    28\t   ends), not guessed. Risk: keys are model-written (`scope_source: model`; old-2 v8 stand-alone CPU has measure `other` and would be\n    29\t   missed; old-3 v14's question says \"total CPU\" while its scope says \"Vera CPU\"). A missed pair costs nothing new; a wrong pair\n    30\t   shows a judge an irrelevant whole, which the judge can weigh.\n    31\t   Not covered, said plainly: growth-rate against total of the same year (council Q's v21, v17: duplicates by D197's idea, a\n    32\t   separate class); FY2028 against FY2027 (a successor reading its base: not an identity of one period).\n    33\t2. **The line.** Print the dependency's stored `reference` and `implied_outcome` (D260 fields, written for every judgement) before\n    34\t   the reasons, so the decisive figure is never cut; keep the reasons cut. Only requests that carry a dependency change; today's\n    35\t   requests carry none, so every stored request stays byte-equal. Code, not the frozen prompt file; still a new judging version.\n    36\t3. **Filing.** A component edge moves no statement: `narrowest_links` reads only edges whose kind states a hierarchy (seed edges).\n    37\t   The 106 double-filed items stay as they are today. The edge needs a stored kind; old product stores have no rows, seeded stores\n    38\t   keep their marks (SEPARATION-DESIGN 2.3).\n    39\t4. **D542's five items in the product:** awaited circle: does not arise (code-written edges need no waiting; a circle would need a\n    40\t   whole reading its part, which the rule never writes; the circle check stays). Closing: the reader prints \"closed\" today; a part and\n    41\t   its whole share the fiscal year, so they close together or the part reads the closing conclusion; \"historical only\" is not needed.\n    42\t   Theme twice: the rule names number questions of one company, never a theme. Historical readers: they read \"depends on\" correctly\n    43\t   for a read edge; product stores hold no old rows. Label: `last_end` exists only on seeded stores; the product's label is computed.\n    44\t5. **Order and cost:** the whole is judged first (`topological`), a changed whole queues its parts (`queued_by_change`). A few extra\n    45\t   judge calls a day at about $0.006 each (the probe's measured cost): cents.\n    46\t6. **Pieces and test.** Touched: the matcher's writer (an edge after matching), judging's line (code), filing's narrowest reader\n    47\t   (code), the store (a kind). All frozen as poc-v118 runs them: a new version Alex opens. The test: because filing and matching are\n    48\t   unchanged, only the parts' judgements change; replay each draw from its archive with every other answer reused byte-equal, and\n    49\t   judge the linked parts forward day by day as their own sequence, beside a control sequence of the same parts unlinked (fresh,\n    50\t   so the sampler is measured). About 2–3 parts a draw × about 75 days × 2 arms × 3 draws ≈ 1,000 calls ≈ $6 (estimate). Pass:\n    51\t   reconciliation by the probe's reading rule on a fixed set of days, and no answer moved away from a source-backed figure.\n    52\t   Unknown to check before: whether any other request reads a part's conclusion (reading step's shown questions, theme block).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/self-reference/RESULT.md\nnl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/reference-census.md\nnl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/self-reference/reference-census.md'","aggregated_output":"     1\t# The self-made market reference: class, mechanism and share (D692; 2026-11-21; $0)\n     2\t\n     3\tAsked by D692: \"the self-made reference is traced apart on stored answers, at $0\". Nothing was sent and nothing changed.\n     4\tCensus: `reference_census.py` → `reference-census.md` (the three finished poc-v118 draws, read-only; positive control old-2 v9 on\n     5\t2026-09-15 is marked).\n     6\t\n     7\t## The class\n     8\tjudging-v7 asks every judgement for a `reference`: \"what the market expects for this question (consensus, the company's guidance, the\n     9\tstated plan or deadline)\". Over the number questions of the three draws (54 questions, 2,375 judgements that have a previous one):\n    10\t\n    11\t| draw | the reference's first figure is in no part of the request outside the previous conclusion | of which the reference says it was carried from the previous judgement |\n    12\t|---|---|---|\n    13\t| old-1 | 28 (3%) | 15 (2%): v1 credit support 9, v8 Data Center 5, v2 1 |\n    14\t| old-2 | 55 (7%) | 29 (4%): v9 Data Center 28, v15 1 |\n    15\t| old-3 | 11 (2%) | 0 |\n    16\t\n    17\tThe second column is the defect: a figure the system computed itself, presented the next day as the market's (\"The carried-forward\n    18\tmarket-reference proxy is about $372.5 billion\", old-1 v8; \"Market consensus is approximately $372 billion, the reference supplied in\n    19\tthe previous conclusion\", old-2 v9 on 09-12). The rest of the first column, read on a sample (old-1 v2, old-2 v1 and v2, old-3 v33),\n    20\tis mostly a reference built from disclosed company figures and labelled as such (\"No consensus ... is supplied. The closest disclosed\n    21\treference is the $8.38 billion subtotal of the $3.5 billion ... and Sharon AI's $4.88 billion\"): not the defect. The strict class is\n    22\tsmall (44 of 2,375, 1.9%) but it sits on the FY2027 Data Center question in two of three draws, the question council Q read first, and\n    23\tit lasts: in old-2 from 08-16 to the end of the run.\n    24\t\n    25\t## The mechanism, traced on old-2 v9 (every judgement 07-06 to 09-20 read)\n    26\t1. **07-06 to 07-21:** \"No market consensus or company FY2027 guidance is supplied\"; from 07-10 it uses the closest company figure,\n    27\t   the $91B Q2 total-revenue guide times the Data Center mix. Correct behaviour.\n    28\t2. **07-22 to 08-15:** \"No full-year FY2027 Data Center consensus or company guidance is supplied. The available annual run-rate\n    29\t   reference is about $372B\" (FY2026's $193.7B carried at Q1's 92% growth): its own calculation, still labelled as one.\n    30\t3. **08-16 onward:** the request shows the previous conclusion as its rung and reasons only (`views/judging.py` line 157, cut at 800\n    31\t   characters; the `reference` field is not shown). The reasons say \"The reference is approximately $372 billion\"; the next answer\n    32\t   calls it \"the market expectation stated in the previous conclusion\" (08-18), then \"Market consensus is approximately $372 billion\"\n    33\t   (08-28).\n    34\t4. **09-14:** the reasons drop the $372B sentence and keep only \"the approximately $414 billion forecast\" (its own estimate since\n    35\t   09-11, built on a SemiAnalysis H2 uplift). **09-15:** \"Approximately $414 billion is the reference expectation\". It stays to 09-20\n    36\t   (\"The market reference supplied by the previous conclusion is approximately $414 billion\").\n    37\t\n    38\tThe request sentences: judging-v7 line 3 says \"The previous conclusion is supplied only for comparison\"; line 4 asks for \"what the\n    39\tmarket expects\". No sentence says what to write when the material holds no market figure, and the previous conclusion carries no mark\n    40\tof where its figures came from, so the judge's own figure re-enters as a given. Prompt-audit verdicts: **missing** (no case for \"no\n    41\tmarket figure supplied\") and **misread** (the comparison-only previous conclusion used as a source); the model's own account was not\n    42\tasked (a cent a case).\n    43\t\n    44\t## Why the Data Center question had no market figure\n    45\tThe total-revenue question v14 cites a real one from 09-14: \"The latest cited Wall Street estimate is $411 billion (e4061)\", then\n    46\te4097 and e4348. Those statements are filed under total revenue only (one home, D207), and v9 does not read v14: the 09-20 request for\n    47\tv9 holds no \"411\" (`../dependency-probe/run/control-request-user.txt`). In the probe the linked request delivered v14's conclusion,\n    48\tand one of the three linked answers dropped the $414B and derived its reference from the $411B (changed 1, `claude-marks.md`); the\n    49\tother two kept \"$414B\", which their previous conclusion still stated.\n    50\t\n    51\t## What would remove it (candidates, not decided; the judge is frozen, so each is a new version Alex opens)\n    52\t| Candidate | What it does | Share of the strict class (these draws) |\n    53\t|---|---|---|\n    54\t| linking related questions (under review, `../dependency-design/`) | delivers the whole's market figure to the part | the Data Center cases, 33 of 44; not credit support (old-1 v1, 9). A carried figure already in the previous conclusion can still win (2 of 3 in the probe) |\n    55\t| a sourced reference: the answer names the evidence or dependency its reference comes from, or states that none was supplied; code checks that the named source was shown (identity, not importance) | stops an own figure being presented as the market's, wherever it arises | the whole class by construction; unproven until sent |\n    56\t| show the previous reference with a mark \"our own figure\" | a label on one path | a patch: the reasons text carries the same figure unmarked |\n    57\t\n    58\tNext: this goes to the council with the dependency design review, then to Alex with it; no send before that.\nnl: docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/reference-census.md: No such file or directory\n     1\t# Self-made market reference: census on the three finished poc-v118 draws ($0)\n     2\t\n     3\tGenerated by `reference_census.py`. Number questions only (unit USD or percent). \"carried\": the reference says it was taken\n     4\tfrom the previous judgement; \"own value\": its first figure equals the previous judgement's implied outcome (the system's own\n     5\testimate); \"unsourced\": its first figure is nowhere in the request the judge was sent, outside the previous conclusion.\n     6\tAll are read from the stored fields and requests; none says the figure is wrong, only where it came from.\n     7\t\n     8\t| draw | number questions | judgements with a previous one | carried | own value | unsourced | own value and unsourced | carried and unsourced |\n     9\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n    10\t| old-1 | 19 | 821 | 30 (4%) | 273 (33%) | 28 (3%) | 5 (1%) | 15 (2%) |\n    11\t| old-2 | 17 | 823 | 49 (6%) | 231 (28%) | 55 (7%) | 9 (1%) | 29 (4%) |\n    12\t| old-3 | 18 | 731 | 1 (0%) | 261 (36%) | 11 (2%) | 7 (1%) | 0 (0%) |\n    13\t\n    14\t## old-1: per question\n    15\t\n    16\t| question | judged | with previous | carried | own value | unsourced | carried and unsourced | first unsourced day | text |\n    17\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n    18\t| v2 | 68 | 67 | 1 | 7 | 12 | 1 | 2026-07-14 | What total amount of NVIDIA’s credit-support and capacity-purchase obligations w |\n    19\t| v1 | 68 | 67 | 9 | 15 | 9 | 9 | 2026-08-02 | How much credit support for AI clouds will NVIDIA have committed at the end of F |\n    20\t| v8 | 75 | 74 | 13 | 1 | 5 | 5 | 2026-07-27 | How much Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027? |\n    21\t| v28 | 35 | 34 | 0 | 5 | 2 | 0 | 2026-09-19 | How much will NVIDIA’s committed equity-investment obligations to ecosystem part |\n    22\t| v11 | 64 | 63 | 0 | 25 | 0 | 0 | - | What gross margin will NVIDIA report for FY2027? |\n    23\t| v14 | 55 | 54 | 0 | 5 | 0 | 0 | - | How much will NVIDIA’s supply-chain purchase commitments outstanding be at the e |\n    24\t| v15 | 55 | 54 | 0 | 39 | 0 | 0 | - | How much total CPU revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027? |\n    25\t| v18 | 44 | 43 | 0 | 43 | 0 | 0 | - | How much financing will NVIDIA have provided or committed to Amkor under the pac |\n    26\t| v32 | 26 | 25 | 0 | 25 | 0 | 0 | - | How much will NVIDIA’s outstanding payment obligation for the Poolside Model Fac |\n    27\t| v34 | 22 | 21 | 0 | 9 | 0 | 0 | - | What gross margin will NVIDIA report for FY2028? |\n    28\t| v36 | 18 | 17 | 0 | 17 | 0 | 0 | - | How much financing will NVIDIA have provided to MediaTek through the announced c |\n    29\t| v38 | 18 | 17 | 0 | 16 | 0 | 0 | - | How much will NVIDIA’s MediaTek convertible-bond purchase obligation amount to a |\n    30\t| v4 | 80 | 79 | 0 | 4 | 0 | 0 | - | What will NVIDIA's total revenue be in FY2027? |\n    31\t| v40 | 17 | 16 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | - | How much will NVIDIA's total revenue grow year over year in FY2028? |\n    32\t| v42 | 12 | 11 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | - | How much Networking revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027? |\n    33\t| v44 | 11 | 10 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | - | How much Vera CPU revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2028? |\n    34\t| v5 | 75 | 74 | 3 | 19 | 0 | 0 | - | What will NVIDIA's total revenue be in FY2028? |\n    35\t| v6 | 51 | 50 | 0 | 18 | 0 | 0 | - | How much will the four largest AI hyperscalers spend on data center capital expe |\n    36\t| v7 | 46 | 45 | 4 | 25 | 0 | 0 | - | How much will the four largest