{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^## D69[0-9]|reference-census|reference trace'\"' docs/DECISIONS-log.md docs/CURRENT_STATE.md\nnl -ba src/hivemind/views/matching.py | sed -n '58,109p'\nnl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-probe/reading-rule.md | sed -n '12,36p'\"","aggregated_output":"docs/CURRENT_STATE.md:464:  separation, D538's filing changes) with the council, then Alex; the self-made $414B reference traced apart.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:10360:## D690 · 2026-11-20 · Alex chooses A: poc-v118 is the product, the research line rests until his new direction; the D681–D689 records are committed locally\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:10375:## D691 · 2026-11-20 · Alex chooses A after council Q: no daily wrapper yet; link related questions first, a $0 check then a few cents\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:10398:## D692 · 2026-11-20 · Under Alex's A (D691): the dependency probe passes its registered rule; the dependency design review reopens at $0\n    58\tNUMBER_WITH_UNIT = re.compile(r'(-?\\d+(?:[.,]\\d+)?)\\s*(万亿|亿|百万|%|trillion|billion|million|tn|bn|mn)?', re.I)\n    59\tYEAR_LIKE = re.compile(r'(?:FY|财年)\\s*\\d{4}|\\d{4}\\s*(?:年|财年)|\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}')\n    60\tSCALE = {'万亿': 1e4, 'trillion': 1e3, 'tn': 1e3, 'million': 1e-3, 'mn': 1e-3}      # 亿 and billion are the unscaled magnitudes of their language\n    61\t\n    62\t\n    63\tdef first_value(condition):\n    64\t    \"\"\"The first quantity in a rung condition, years removed, magnitudes brought to one scale within a language.\"\"\"\n    65\t    for found in NUMBER_WITH_UNIT.finditer(YEAR_LIKE.sub(' ', condition or '')):\n    66\t        value = float(found.group(1).replace(',', ''))\n    67\t        unit = (found.group(2) or '').lower()\n    68\t        return value * SCALE.get(unit, 1)\n    69\t    return None\n    70\t\n    71\t\n    72\tdef ladder_direction(rungs):\n    73\t    \"\"\"+1 when the quantities rise from the first rung to the last, -1 when they fall, None when undecidable. The rungs'\n    74\t    numeric bounds decide when both ends carry them; the prose is read only for a ladder without bounds.\"\"\"\n    75\t    first, last = rungs[0], rungs[-1]\n    76\t    if any(r.get('lo') is not None or r.get('hi') is not None for r in rungs):\n    77\t        if first.get('hi') is not None and last.get('lo') is not None and float(first['hi']) <= float(last['lo']):\n    78\t            return 1\n    79\t        if first.get('lo') is not None and last.get('hi') is not None and float(last['hi']) <= float(first['lo']):\n    80\t            return -1\n    81\t        return None\n    82\t    numbers = [first_value(rung['condition']) for rung in rungs]\n    83\t    known = [n for n in numbers if n is not None]\n    84\t    if len(known) < 2 or known[0] == known[-1]:\n    85\t        return None\n    86\t    return 1 if known[0] < known[-1] else -1\n    87\t\n    88\t\n    89\t@dataclasses.dataclass\n    90\tclass Lists:\n    91\t    candidate_lists: dict      # candidate id -> [view_id]\n    92\t    evidence_lists: dict       # (evidence handover id, view_id) -> [evidence_id]\n    93\t\n    94\t\n    95\tCJK_RUN = re.compile(r'[一-鿿]+')\n    96\t\n    97\t\n    98\tdef _words(text):\n    99\t    \"\"\"Tokens for the within-view ranking: latin words and numbers, and character bigrams for Chinese runs (a\n   100\t    Chinese one-line has no spaces, so whole clauses would otherwise be single tokens that never overlap).\"\"\"\n   101\t    text = (text or '').lower()\n   102\t    words = set(re.findall(r'[a-z0-9]+(?:[.,][0-9]+)?%?', text))\n   103\t    for run in CJK_RUN.findall(text):\n   104\t        words.update(run[i:i + 2] for i in range(len(run) - 1))\n   105\t    return words\n   106\t\n   107\t\n   108\tdef rank_evidence(conn, view_id, one_line, top_n):\n   109\t    \"\"\"The view's evidence in force ranked by word overlap with the new piece's one-line (the within-view search).\"\"\"\n    12\t## The reading rule (fixed before any answer)\n    13\tFor each answer, two readers (Claude first, then you blind to the arm under shuffled labels, given the answer, v14's 09-20 conclusion\n    14\tand the request's evidence) record:\n    15\t- **A.** Its FY2027 Data Center estimate and its Q3 and Q4 FY2027 Data Center estimates, as stated or as its own arithmetic gives them.\n    16\t- **B.** Whether its arithmetic adds up (its quarters sum to its year within $2B).\n    17\t- **C.** Whether each assumption is disclosed and grounded in its own request (a figure, guidance or growth rate that request\n    18\t  contains: the evidence listed, and v14's shown conclusion only in the changed arm); a step with no source in its request is\n    19\t  unsupported.\n    20\t- **D.** Room for the rest of NVIDIA: v14's figures minus the Data Center figures leave at least $25B for FY2027 and at least $6B\n    21\t  in each of Q3 and Q4. These floors are this test's assumptions, taken from the reported non-Data-Center revenue in the request\n    22\t  (Q1 $6.35B, Q2 $7.2B, first half $13.55B). Both arms are measured against v14's 09-20 figures ($419B FY, $113.5B Q3, $127B Q4),\n    23\t  whether or not the answer saw them.\n    24\t- **E.** (changed arm only, apart) whether v14's forecast bounds or changes its calculation (a v14 figure used in its arithmetic or\n    25\t  as a stated ceiling); a citation or a mention alone is recorded as \"noticed\", not \"used\".\n    26\t\n    27\t**Reconciles** = A gives all three figures, B, C and D all hold. A missing Q3 or Q4 estimate = \"not tested\", never a pass.\n    28\t\n    29\t- **Pass:** changed reconciles in at least 2 of 3; control reconciles in at most 1 of 3; no added refusal (first attempts compared).\n    30\t- **Inconclusive:** control reconciles in 2 or 3 of 3 (the stored contradiction is a coin flip here), or changed has 2 or more\n    31\t  \"not tested\".\n    32\t- **Fail:** otherwise. A fail says this input did not reliably help; it does not locate the cause.\n    33\t- Where the two readers differ on a point, the source decides, both marks recorded.\n    34\t\n    35\t**What it decides:** pass → reopen the dependency design review (D542's five items, the `reads`/`supports` separation, D538's seven\n    36\tfiling changes) with the council, then Alex; fail or inconclusive → report to Alex, no further send without a new design.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/self-reference/reference_census.py | sed -n '1,160p'\nrg -n 'def ladder|ASSET_LABELS|favourable|bullish' src/hivemind/{extraction,vocabulary}.py\nrg -n '2\\\\.|later|new item' docs/research/2026-10-26-theme-dependencies/design.md | head -24\nnl -ba src/hivemind/views/matching.py | sed -n '153,174p;327,375p'\nnl -ba src/hivemind/views/judging.py | sed -n '136,172p'\nnl -ba docs/prd/06-views.md | sed -n '117,144p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/self-reference/reference_census.py | sed -n '1,160p'\nrg -n 'def ladder|ASSET_LABELS|favourable|bullish' src/hivemind/{extraction,vocabulary}.py\nrg -n '2\\\\.|later|new item' docs/research/2026-10-26-theme-dependencies/design.md | head -24\nnl -ba src/hivemind/views/matching.py | sed -n '153,174p;327,375p'\nnl -ba src/hivemind/views/judging.py | sed -n '136,172p'\nnl -ba docs/prd/06-views.md | sed -n '117,144p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t\"\"\"$0 census of the self-made market reference (D692): in the three finished poc-v118 draws, how often a judgement's `reference`\n     2\t(the field judging-v7 asks for: \"what the market expects for this question (consensus, the company's guidance, the stated plan or\n     3\tdeadline)\") is the system's own earlier figure rather than a market figure.\n     4\t\n     5\tTwo measures, per judgement of a question that already has a previous judgement:\n     6\t  carried:   the reference says it was taken from the previous judgement or conclusion (the words \"previous\", \"prior\" or \"carried\");\n     7\t  own_value: the reference's first figure equals the first figure of the previous judgement's `implied_outcome` (the system's own\n     8\t             estimate), within 0.5% (the same unit word: billion, trillion, million or percent).\n     9\t  unsourced: no figure in the request the judge was sent equals the reference's first figure, outside the \"[Previous conclusion\"\n    10\t             section (the stored request, found in the draw's archive by the judgement's request_sha256). A figure the evidence\n    11\t             states (a signed amount, a guidance figure, a rung bound) is therefore not counted, whatever the estimate equals.\n    12\tA judgement counts once per measure. The stores are opened read-only. The positive control is old-2 v9 on 2026-09-15 (reference\n    13\t\"$414 billion\", the 09-14 implied outcome \"$414 billion\", not in the evidence shown): the script exits with an error unless\n    14\tboth own_value and unsourced mark it.\n    15\t\n    16\t  python3 reference_census.py > reference-census.md\n    17\t\"\"\"\n    18\timport re\n    19\timport sqlite3\n    20\timport sys\n    21\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    22\t\n    23\tREPO = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[4]\n    24\tRUNS = REPO / 'poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run'\n    25\tFIGURE = re.compile(r'\\$?\\s?(\\d+(?:,\\d{3})*(?:\\.\\d+)?)\\s?(trillion|billion|million|bn|B\\b|T\\b|%|percent)', re.IGNORECASE)\n    26\tUNIT = {'trillion': 1e12, 't': 1e12, 'billion': 1e9, 'bn': 1e9, 'b': 1e9, 'million': 1e6, '%': 1.0, 'percent': 1.0}\n    27\tCARRIED = re.compile(r'\\b(previous|prior|carried)\\b', re.IGNORECASE)\n    28\t\n    29\t\n    30\tdef first_figure(text):\n    31\t    match = FIGURE.search(text or '')\n    32\t    if not match:\n    33\t        return None\n    34\t    unit = match.group(2).lower()\n    35\t    kind = 'percent' if unit in ('%', 'percent') else 'amount'\n    36\t    return kind, float(match.group(1).replace(',', '')) * UNIT[unit]\n    37\t\n    38\t\n    39\tdef same(a, b):\n    40\t    return a and b and a[0] == b[0] and abs(a[1] - b[1]) <= 0.005 * max(abs(a[1]), abs(b[1]), 1e-9)\n    41\t\n    42\t\n    43\tdef all_figures(text):\n    44\t    for match in FIGURE.finditer(text or ''):\n    45\t        unit = match.group(2).lower()\n    46\t        yield ('percent' if unit in ('%', 'percent') else 'amount'), float(match.group(1).replace(',', '')) * UNIT[unit]\n    47\t\n    48\t\n    49\tdef without_previous_conclusion(user_text):\n    50\t    \"\"\"The request's user text with the \"[Previous conclusion\" section removed (it runs to the next bracketed header or the end).\"\"\"\n    51\t    return re.sub(r'\\n\\[Previous conclusion[^\\n]*(?:\\n(?!\\[)[^\\n]*)*', '\\n', user_text)\n    52\t\n    53\t\n    54\tdef shown_material(archive, request_sha256):\n    55\t    row = archive.execute(\"select request_json from model_calls where request_sha256=? limit 1\", (request_sha256,)).fetchone()\n    56\t    if not row:\n    57\t        raise SystemExit(f'request {request_sha256} not in the archive: the census cannot judge it')\n    58\t    import json\n    59\t    messages = json.loads(row[0])['messages']\n    60\t    return without_previous_conclusion(messages[-1]['content'])\n    61\t\n    62\t\n    63\tdef census(draw):\n    64\t    conn = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{RUNS / draw}/prod/views.sqlite?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    65\t    archive = sqlite3.connect(f'file:{RUNS / draw}/prod/archive.sqlite?mode=ro', uri=True)\n    66\t    questions = dict(conn.execute('select view_id, question from views'))\n    67\t    units = dict(conn.execute('select view_id, unit from view_keys'))\n    68\t    rows = conn.execute('select view_id, judgement_id, publication_day, reference, implied_outcome, request_sha256 from judgements order by view_id, judgement_id').fetchall()\n    69\t    per_question, marked, previous = {}, [], {}\n    70\t    for view_id, judgement_id, day, reference, implied, request_sha256 in rows:\n    71\t        if units.get(view_id) not in ('USD', 'percent'):\n    72\t            continue\n    73\t        stats = per_question.setdefault(view_id, {'judged': 0, 'with_previous': 0, 'carried': 0, 'own_value': 0, 'unsourced': 0, 'carried_unsourced': 0, 'first_unsourced': None})\n    74\t        stats['judged'] += 1\n    75\t        if view_id in previous:\n    76\t            stats['with_previous'] += 1\n    77\t            carried = bool(CARRIED.search(reference or ''))\n    78\t            figure = first_figure(reference)\n    79\t            own = bool(same(figure, first_figure(previous[view_id])))\n    80\t            unsourced = bool(figure) and not any(same(figure, shown) for shown in all_figures(shown_material(archive, request_sha256)))\n    81\t            stats['carried'] += carried\n    82\t            stats['own_value'] += own\n    83\t            stats['unsourced'] += unsourced\n    84\t            stats['carried_unsourced'] += carried and unsourced\n    85\t            if unsourced and not stats['first_unsourced']:\n    86\t                stats['first_unsourced'] = day\n    87\t            marked.append((view_id, day, carried, own, unsourced))\n    88\t        previous[view_id] = implied\n    89\t    return questions, per_question, marked\n    90\t\n    91\t\n    92\tdef main():\n    93\t    print('# Self-made market reference: census on the three finished poc-v118 draws ($0)\\n')\n    94\t    print('Generated by `reference_census.py`. Number questions only (unit USD or percent). \"carried\": the reference says it was taken')\n    95\t    print('from the previous judgement; \"own value\": its first figure equals the previous judgement\\'s implied outcome (the system\\'s own')\n    96\t    print('estimate); \"unsourced\": its first figure is nowhere in the request the judge was sent, outside the previous conclusion.')\n    97\t    print('All are read from the stored fields and requests; none says the figure is wrong, only where it came from.\\n')\n    98\t    print('| draw | number questions | judgements with a previous one | carried | own value | unsourced | own value and unsourced | carried and unsourced |')\n    99\t    print('|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|')\n   100\t    details = {}\n   101\t    control = False\n   102\t    for draw in ('old-1', 'old-2', 'old-3'):\n   103\t        questions, per_question, marked = census(draw)\n   104\t        details[draw] = (questions, per_question)\n   105\t        with_previous = sum(s['with_previous'] for s in per_question.values())\n   106\t        counts = [sum(1 for row in marked if test(row)) for test in (lambda r: r[2], lambda r: r[3], lambda r: r[4], lambda r: r[3] and r[4], lambda r: r[2] and r[4])]\n   107\t        print(f'| {draw} | {len(per_question)} | {with_previous} | ' + ' | '.join(f'{n} ({n / max(with_previous, 1):.0%})' for n in counts) + ' |')\n   108\t        if draw == 'old-2':\n   109\t            control = any(row[0] == 'v9' and row[1] == '2026-09-15' and row[3] and row[4] for row in marked)\n   110\t    for draw, (questions, per_question) in details.items():\n   111\t        print(f'\\n## {draw}: per question\\n')\n   112\t        print('| question | judged | with previous | carried | own value | unsourced | carried and unsourced | first unsourced day | text |')\n   113\t        print('|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|')\n   114\t        for view_id, s in sorted(per_question.items(), key=lambda kv: -kv[1]['unsourced']):\n   115\t            print(f'| {view_id} | {s[\"judged\"]} | {s[\"with_previous\"]} | {s[\"carried\"]} | {s[\"own_value\"]} | {s[\"unsourced\"]} | {s[\"carried_unsourced\"]} | {s[\"first_unsourced\"] or \"-\"} | {questions.get(view_id, \"?\")[:80]} |')\n   116\t    if not control:\n   117\t        sys.exit('positive control failed: old-2 v9 on 2026-09-15 is not marked as both its own value and unsourced')\n   118\t    print('\\nPositive control: old-2 v9 on 2026-09-15 is marked \"own value\" and \"unsourced\".')\n   119\t\n   120\t\n   121\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n   122\t    main()\nsrc/hivemind/vocabulary.py:13:DIRECTIONS = ['first_is_bullish', 'last_is_bullish', 'same', 'opposite']\nsrc/hivemind/vocabulary.py:14:ASSET_LABELS = ['Strongly bullish', 'Bullish', 'Neutral', 'Bearish', 'Strongly bearish']\nsrc/hivemind/vocabulary.py:23:    'direction': {'对方第一格是看多': 'first_is_bullish', '对方最后一格是看多': 'last_is_bullish', '同向': 'same', '反向': 'opposite'},\nsrc/hivemind/vocabulary.py:24:    'label': {'强烈看多': 'Strongly bullish', '看多': 'Bullish', '中性': 'Neutral', '看空': 'Bearish', '强烈看空': 'Strongly bearish', '是': 'Yes', '否': 'No'},\nsrc/hivemind/extraction.py:408:OBJECT_LABELS = vocabulary.ASSET_LABELS\nsrc/hivemind/extraction.py:413:    Strongly bullish (the model often orders a revenue ladder by rising value) is the same ladder; normalise_ladder\nsrc/hivemind/extraction.py:427:    \"\"\"Position 1 is Strongly bullish (06-views): a reversed asset ladder is turned round, label and condition together.\"\"\"\n59:### 2. When a theme thesis opens\n68:Codex proposed a third lifecycle state (\"pending candidate\" kept for later retrieval). Not adopted: it adds a state and a\n73:### 3. How later items add links\n75:- A later company item whose model reads a theme in its shown list (block 5 shows the theme theses linked to the\n144:| cycle check before an edge | unchanged; also on a later-added edge and on binding an awaited key |\n146:| rejudge order: dependencies before dependants | unchanged; a later-added edge enters the same ordering |\n157:   role version would open it from the same call. A later MU or AMD item on the same stage adds its own link and sign.\n158:2. **Hyperscaler capex 2026 → NVDA data-center revenue; MSFT capex as a component.** The Feb 25 call opens the\n164:   later item reports), and records the question for Alex.\n167:   favourable: lower); each binds when that company's thesis exists; each company's later item may correct its sign.\n180:2. Allow a dependency to be added to an existing thesis by a later item (changes 06-views \"only when B is created\").\n200:  added later (point 2), and keep the cycle check.\n244:2. **The answer.** The judgement schema for v4 gains `theme_pushes: [{view_id, push}]`, `push` in the existing `PUSHES` enum\n280:8. **Explicit dependencies are unchanged**, including D191 point 2 (a dependency added to an existing thesis later), which\n347:2. Three stored v3 judgement requests of asset theses from r4 (one NVDA data-center revenue, one AMD, one a company whose\n   153\t    for e in handover.evidence:\n   154\t        for view_id in e['links']:\n   155\t            if view_id in candidate_ids:\n   156\t                continue\n   157\t            evidence_lists[(e['id'], view_id)] = rank_evidence(conn, view_id, e['one_line'], top_n)\n   158\t    return Lists(candidate_lists, evidence_lists)\n   159\t\n   160\t\n   161\tdef describe_view(conn, view_id, english=False):\n   162\t    v = store.view(conn, view_id)\n   163\t    successor = conn.execute('select view_id from successions where succeeds=?', (view_id,)).fetchone()\n   164\t    if english:\n   165\t        rungs = ' / '.join(f'{r[\"label\"]}: {r[\"condition\"]}' for r in store.rungs_of(conn, view_id))\n   166\t        state = 'open' if store.is_open(conn, view_id) else 'closed'\n   167\t        tail = f'; successor already exists: {successor[\"view_id\"]}' if successor else ''\n   168\t        groups = store.groups_of_view(conn, view_id)\n   169\t        tail += f'; research group: ' + ', '.join(f'{g[\"group_id\"]} \"{g[\"name\"]}\"' for g in groups) if groups else ''\n   170\t        return f'{view_id} ({state}, {v[\"object_id\"]}, {v[\"kind\"]}, focus \"{v[\"looks_at\"]}\", {v[\"year\"] or \"\"}, due {v[\"due_day\"]}): {v[\"question\"]}\\n    Ladder: {rungs}{tail}'\n   171\t    rungs = ' / '.join(f'{r[\"label\"]}：{r[\"condition\"]}' for r in store.rungs_of(conn, view_id))\n   172\t    state = '开着' if store.is_open(conn, view_id) else '关了'\n   173\t    tail = f'；已有下一期 {successor[\"view_id\"]}' if successor else ''\n   174\t    return f'{view_id}（{state}，{v[\"object_id\"]}，{v[\"kind\"]}，看的是「{v[\"looks_at\"]}」，{v[\"year\"] or \"\"}，到期 {v[\"due_day\"]}）：{v[\"question\"]}\\n    梯子：{rungs}{tail}'\n   327\t                    refusals.append(f'candidate {c[\"id\"]}: {target} can have one successor; {first[\"id\"]} already succeeds it in this answer')\n   328\t                    continue\n   329\t                succession_targets.setdefault(target, c)             # a second wording with the same code-owned key is the same successor (coalesced by batch_plan)\n   330\t                # 06-views: a successor keeps the predecessor's direction; the writer stores a numeric ladder in that direction (the first\n   331\t                # real succession, 2027 hyperscaler capex after 2026, came low-to-high where its predecessor ran high-to-low), so no refusal here\n   332\t        if outcome in ('new', 'succession'):\n   333\t            object_id = universe.resolve(c['object'])\n   334\t            if not object_id:\n   335\t                not_opened[c['id']] = f'object {c[\"object\"]!r} not on the research list'\n   336\t                if c['kind'] == 'theme':\n   337\t                    store.pool(conn, 'suggested_theme', c['object'], {'question': c['question'], 'input_id': None}, 0)\n   338\t                outcomes[c['id']] = ('skip', None, [])\n   339\t                continue\n   340\t            outcomes[c['id']] = (outcome, target or None, [])\n   341\t            raw_deps[c['id']] = d.get('dependencies', [])\n   342\t        elif outcome == 'merge':\n   343\t            outcomes[c['id']] = (outcome, target, [])\n   344\t        else:\n   345\t            outcomes[c['id']] = ('skip', None, [])\n   346\t            not_opened[c['id']] = d.get('reason', '')\n   347\t    # dependencies, once every candidate's outcome is known\n   348\t    opened = {cid for cid, (outcome, _, _) in outcomes.items() if outcome in ('new', 'succession')}\n   349\t    for cid, dependencies in raw_deps.items():\n   350\t        deps = []\n   351\t        bad = False\n   352\t        for dep in dependencies:\n   353\t            view_id, chain, year = dep['view_id'].strip(), dep['wait_chain_view_id'].strip(), dep['wait_year'].strip()\n   354\t            if view_id:\n   355\t                if view_id in candidate_by_id and view_id not in opened:\n   356\t                    refusals.append(f'candidate {cid}: dependency {view_id} is a candidate that is not opened')\n   357\t                    bad = True\n   358\t                    break\n   359\t                if view_id not in listed_all and view_id not in candidate_by_id:\n   360\t                    refusals.append(f'candidate {cid}: dependency {view_id} was not shown')\n   361\t                    bad = True\n   362\t                    break\n   363\t                if view_id == cid:\n   364\t                    refusals.append(f'candidate {cid}: depends on itself')\n   365\t                    bad = True\n   366\t                    break\n   367\t                deps.append({'view_id': view_id, 'wait_chain_view_id': None, 'wait_year': None, 'direction': dep['direction']})\n   368\t            elif chain and year:\n   369\t                if chain not in listed_all and chain not in candidate_by_id:\n   370\t                    refusals.append(f'candidate {cid}: waited chain {chain} was not shown')\n   371\t                    bad = True\n   372\t                    break\n   373\t                deps.append({'view_id': None, 'wait_chain_view_id': chain, 'wait_year': year, 'direction': dep['direction']})\n   374\t        if bad:\n   375\t            continue\n   136\t            lines.append(f'    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read it as a later version of {p[\"revises\"][\"evidence_id\"]} ({p[\"revises\"][\"original_day\"]}); both are in force: {p[\"revises\"][\"one_line\"]}')\n   137\t    if deps:\n   138\t        lines.append('\\n[Current conclusions of the theses it depends on]')\n   139\t        for d in deps:\n   140\t            target = d['resolved_to']\n   141\t            if not target:\n   142\t                lines.append(f'- the {d[\"wait_year\"]} thesis on chain {d[\"wait_chain_view_id\"]}: not yet created ({d[\"direction\"]})')\n   143\t                continue\n   144\t            tv = store.view(conn, target)\n   145\t            state = store.current_state(conn, target)\n   146\t            flag = 'historical only' if d['resolution'] == 'history_only' else ('closed' if not store.is_open(conn, target) else 'open')\n   147\t            rung_label = store.rungs_of(conn, target)[state['rung'] - 1]['label'] if state else 'not judged yet'\n   148\t            lines.append(f'- {target} ({flag}; {d[\"direction\"]}) {tv[\"question\"]}: now rung {state[\"rung\"] if state else \"-\"} {rung_label}; reasons: {(state or {}).get(\"reasons\", \"\")[:600]}')\n   149\t    if themes:\n   150\t        lines.append(f'\\n[Themes in force, {len(themes)}]')\n   151\t        for theme in themes:\n   152\t            tv, state = theme['view'], theme['state']\n   153\t            mark = f'; {UPDATED_MARK}' if theme['updated'] else ''\n   154\t            lines.append(f'- {theme[\"view_id\"]} ({tv[\"object_id\"]}, due {tv[\"due_day\"]}) {tv[\"question\"]}: now rung {state[\"rung\"]} {theme[\"rung_label\"]}; '\n   155\t                         f'judged {state[\"publication_day\"]}{mark}; reasons: {(state[\"reasons\"] or \"\")[:THEME_REASONS_CHARS]}')\n   156\t    if last:\n   157\t        lines.append(f'\\n[Previous conclusion, for comparison only] rung {last[\"rung\"]}; reasons: {last[\"reasons\"][:800]}')\n   158\t    else:\n   159\t        lines.append('\\n[Previous conclusion] none: this is the first judgement, so changed must be true.')\n   160\t    lines.append('\\nAnswer per the JSON schema. cites may name only the evidence ids listed above; '\n   161\t                 + ('cites_views only the dependency thesis ids listed above' if deps else 'cites_views must be empty: this thesis depends on no other thesis')\n   162\t                 + ('; theme_pushes only the theme ids listed above; a theme id goes only in theme_pushes, never in cites or cites_views' if themes else '') + '.')\n   163\t    return lines\n   164\t\n   165\t\n   166\tdef build_prompt(conn, view_id, prompt_version):\n   167\t    require_supported(prompt_version)\n   168\t    v = store.view(conn, view_id)\n   169\t    rungs = store.rungs_of(conn, view_id)\n   170\t    pieces, hidden = evidence_in_view(conn, view_id)\n   171\t    deps = store.dependencies_of(conn, view_id)\n   172\t    last = store.current_state(conn, view_id)\n   117\t```\n   118\tB depends on A | What kind of thesis is A? (For an asset thesis B, state which end of A is bullish for B. For a theme thesis B, state whether their ladders have the same or opposite orientation.)\n   119\t├─ Numeric thesis → Read the specified year's thesis (Example: JPM 2027 net interest income → Fed year-end 2027 rate)\n   120\t│   ├─ A is open → Read A's state and reasons\n   121\t│   ├─ A is closed → Read A's closing state and reasons (The frozen outcome is what B needs; keep reading it)\n   122\t│   └─ A does not exist yet → Wait for it (Record the awaited year on the chain containing the shown thesis. When that year's successor is created, bind the dependency and rejudge B once.)\n   123\t└─ Event thesis → Follow succession (Example: NVDA FY2027 China revenue → chip export licensing to China)\n   124\t    ├─ A is open → Read A's state and reasons\n   125\t    ├─ A is closed with a successor → Read the successor (Record the change. The successor changes B's input, so rejudge B once.)\n   126\t    └─ A is closed without a successor → Read A's closing state and reasons, marked “historical only”\n   127\t```\n   128\t\n   129\t- Theme theses do not judge outcomes as good or bad. Each dependent asset thesis records its direction: rate cuts are bullish for Ethereum and bearish for JPM.\n   130\t- A dependency has one direction. An apparent “good first, bad later” relationship needs an intermediate thesis: steel tariffs raising domestic steel prices and weakening downstream steel demand are separate paths.\n   131\t- Dependencies and the theme block are the two ways theses influence each other; succession only orders periods. B depending on A means B reads A's conclusion. The theme block (D191, D195) shows every open, judged theme thesis to every asset thesis's judgement, one to all, and the judgement states which way each theme it weighed pushes it; no edge is written for it. Keep B's direct evidence separate from dependency states and reasons. A's conclusion can affect B like evidence but is not stored as evidence: external events and statements are evidence, whereas A is our own judgement. Treating it as evidence would let the system convince itself.\n   132\t- Count a statement once. A statement about A is A's evidence, including when two candidates arise from one item. B learns it through A's conclusion. Daily filing gives a statement one home: the narrowest open thesis it bears on, as that thesis's own figure, step or estimate or through the demand, supply, competition or pricing behind its answer, plus the same answer's candidates (D207, D259, D264, D265); the separate coverage-start reading was retired (D370). Dependencies are chosen only when B is created; a later item adding a dependency to an existing thesis is decided (D191 point 2) and to be built (D368).\n   133\t- Rejudge an open thesis when its inputs change: new evidence, replacement, a new link to existing evidence, a dependency declaring a changed conclusion, or (for an asset thesis) a theme thesis declaring one. Additional source references alone do not count. Binding an awaited A or moving to its successor also changes B's inputs. Closed theses do not update. A memo-derived thesis is first judged when evidence first links to it; before that, it and its dependants see “not yet judged”.\n   134\t- The matching call chooses a new thesis's dependencies, stating which conclusions it relies on and each direction (D51). Choose only among searched theses, extraction block-5 theses and candidates opened from the same item; no extra search. Jev, the default matcher, is not asked for them, so new theses do not receive dependencies through the default matcher; building the choice on the Jev path is decided (D368). The historical seed questions are retired (D370). A historical seed's dependency arrow means \"supports\" (D368, by D208): for filing, the supporting (driver) thesis is the narrower one; for judging, the supported (root) thesis reads the supporting theses' conclusions, so drivers and themes are judged before their roots. The judging code reads the stored edge the other way today; the fix is to be built and measured (D368). Completed events are evidence, not dependencies: today's oil price influencing OPEC output is evidence for the OPEC-output thesis.\n   135\t- Before adding an edge or following it to a successor, code checks for cycles. Refuse a cycle and ask the model to correct it; persistent cycles follow normal failure handling. Apparently mutually dependent questions indicate poorly defined theses.\n   136\t<!-- /generated: dependencies -->\n   137\t\n   138\t## Succession: the same focus over successive periods\n   139\t\n   140\t<!-- generated: chain -->\n   141\t- Successive periods of the same focus form a chain, such as Fed year-end 2026 rate → 2027 rate → 2028 rate. The chain records period order. Dependency traversal follows the rules above.\n   142\t- One thesis has at most one successor: FY2026 cannot produce two FY2027 successors.\n   143\t- Keep ladder orientation across succession: a strongly bullish first rung remains strongly bullish, although thresholds can change. Dependencies retain their direction; reversing the ends would break it.\n   144\t<!-- /generated: chain -->\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c '\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport sqlite3,json\nbase=Path(\\\"poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run\\\")\ndef db(p):\n return sqlite3.connect(p.resolve().as_uri()+\\\"?mode=ro&immutable=1\\\",uri=True)\nfor draw,ids in ((\\\"old-2\\\",(\\\"v9\\\",\\\"v14\\\")),(\\\"old-1\\\",(\\\"v1\\\",\\\"v4\\\",\\\"v8\\\"))):\n p=base/draw/\\\"prod\\\"\n print(draw)\n with db(p/\\\"views.sqlite\\\") as c, db(p/\\\"archive.sqlite\\\") as a:\n  for v in ids:\n   print(v,c.execute(\\\"select question,created_seq,kind,object_kind from views where view_id=?\\\",(v,)).fetchone(),c.execute(\\\"select position,label,lo,hi from rungs where view_id=? order by position\\\",(v,)).fetchall())\n  if draw==\\\"old-1\\\":\n   for r in c.execute(\\\"select publication_day,reference,implied_outcome from judgements where view_id=? and publication_day between ? and ? order by judgement_id\\\",(\\\"v1\\\",\\\"2026-08-02\\\",\\\"2026-08-04\\\")):\n    print(r)\n   continue\n  common=c.execute(\\\"select count(distinct a.evidence_id),min(a.seq),min(b.seq),max(a.seq),max(b.seq) from evidence_links a join evidence_links b using(evidence_id) where a.view_id=? and b.view_id=?\\\",ids).fetchone()\n  print(\\\"common\\\",common)\n  print(\\\"e ids\\\",c.execute(\\\"select e.evidence_id,e.original_who,e.quote,group_concat(l.view_id) from evidence e join evidence_links l using(evidence_id) where e.evidence_id in (?, ?, ?, ?) group by e.evidence_id\\\",(\\\"e4061\\\",\\\"e4097\\\",\\\"e4348\\\",\\\"e195\\\")).fetchall())\n  for start,end in ((\\\"2026-07-10\\\",\\\"2026-07-12\\\"),(\\\"2026-09-14\\\",\\\"2026-09-20\\\"),(\\\"2026-09-19\\\",\\\"2026-09-20\\\")):\n   it=ot=n=0\n   for v,day,seq,call,reference,outcome,changed in c.execute(\\\"select view_id,publication_day,seq,call_id,reference,implied_outcome,changed from judgements where view_id in (?,?) and publication_day between ? and ? order by judgement_id\\\",(*ids,start,end)):\n    inp,out = a.execute(\\\"select input_tokens,output_tokens from model_calls where call_id=?\\\",(call,)).fetchone()\n    it+=inp; ot+=out;n+=1\n    if end\"'!=\"2026-09-20\" or start==\"2026-09-14\":\n     print(day,v,inp,out,changed,reference,outcome)\n   print(start,end,n,it,ot,6*(0.1*it+0.5*ot)/1e6)\n'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c '\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport sqlite3,json\nbase=Path(\\\"poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run\\\")\ndef db(p):\n return sqlite3.connect(p.resolve().as_uri()+\\\"?mode=ro&immutable=1\\\",uri=True)\nfor draw,ids in ((\\\"old-2\\\",(\\\"v9\\\",\\\"v14\\\")),(\\\"old-1\\\",(\\\"v1\\\",\\\"v4\\\",\\\"v8\\\"))):\n p=base/draw/\\\"prod\\\"\n print(draw)\n with db(p/\\\"views.sqlite\\\") as c, db(p/\\\"archive.sqlite\\\") as a:\n  for v in ids:\n   print(v,c.execute(\\\"select question,created_seq,kind,object_kind from views where view_id=?\\\",(v,)).fetchone(),c.execute(\\\"select position,label,lo,hi from rungs where view_id=? order by position\\\",(v,)).fetchall())\n  if draw==\\\"old-1\\\":\n   for r in c.execute(\\\"select publication_day,reference,implied_outcome from judgements where view_id=? and publication_day between ? and ? order by judgement_id\\\",(\\\"v1\\\",\\\"2026-08-02\\\",\\\"2026-08-04\\\")):\n    print(r)\n   continue\n  common=c.execute(\\\"select count(distinct a.evidence_id),min(a.seq),min(b.seq),max(a.seq),max(b.seq) from evidence_links a join evidence_links b using(evidence_id) where a.view_id=? and b.view_id=?\\\",ids).fetchone()\n  print(\\\"common\\\",common)\n  print(\\\"e ids\\\",c.execute(\\\"select e.evidence_id,e.original_who,e.quote,group_concat(l.view_id) from evidence e join evidence_links l using(evidence_id) where e.evidence_id in (?, ?, ?, ?) group by e.evidence_id\\\",(\\\"e4061\\\",\\\"e4097\\\",\\\"e4348\\\",\\\"e195\\\")).fetchall())\n  for start,end in ((\\\"2026-07-10\\\",\\\"2026-07-12\\\"),(\\\"2026-09-14\\\",\\\"2026-09-20\\\"),(\\\"2026-09-19\\\",\\\"2026-09-20\\\")):\n   it=ot=n=0\n   for v,day,seq,call,reference,outcome,changed in c.execute(\\\"select view_id,publication_day,seq,call_id,reference,implied_outcome,changed from judgements where view_id in (?,?) and publication_day between ? and ? order by judgement_id\\\",(*ids,start,end)):\n    inp,out = a.execute(\\\"select input_tokens,output_tokens from model_calls where call_id=?\\\",(call,)).fetchone()\n    it+=inp; ot+=out;n+=1\n    if end\"'!=\"2026-09-20\" or start==\"2026-09-14\":\n     print(day,v,inp,out,changed,reference,outcome)\n   print(start,end,n,it,ot,6*(0.1*it+0.5*ot)/1e6)\n'\"'\"","aggregated_output":"old-2\nv9 ('How much Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?', 62, 'asset', 'company') [(1, 'Strongly bullish', 450000000000.0, None), (2, 'Bullish', 400000000000.0, 450000000000.0), (3, 'Neutral', 350000000000.0, 400000000000.0), (4, 'Bearish', 300000000000.0, 350000000000.0), (5, 'Strongly bearish', None, 300000000000.0)]\nv14 ('How much total revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?', 148, 'asset', 'company') [(1, 'Strongly bullish', 450000000000.0, None), (2, 'Bullish', 400000000000.0, 450000000000.0), (3, 'Neutral', 350000000000.0, 400000000000.0), (4, 'Bearish', 300000000000.0, 350000000000.0), (5, 'Strongly bearish', None, 300000000000.0)]\ncommon (106, 185, 185, 1853, 1853)\ne ids [('e195', 'Bloomberg', 'The chipmaker is projected to deliver $228 billion in profits on sales of $393 billion in fiscal 2027, which ends Jan. 31. That would represent an expansion of 90% and 82%, respectively, according to data compiled by Bloomberg.', 'v14'), ('e4061', 'Analysts', \"Analysts expect Nvidia's revenue to land at $411 billion in fiscal 2027, an increase of almost 60x in a decade.\", 'v14'), ('e4097', 'Wall Street analysts', 'For FY 2027 (ending in January 2027), Wall Street analysts expect $411 billion in revenue.', 'v14'), ('e4348', 'Analysts', 'Analysts currently project $411 billion in revenue for fiscal 2027, followed by a 65% jump to $678 billion in fiscal 2028.', 'v14,v17,v21,v35')]\n2026-07-10 v14 1920 972 1 Bloomberg-compiled projections expect FY2027 sales of $393 billion, which is rung 3 ($350 billion to less than $400 billion). About $393 billion for FY2027, using Bloomberg’s direct sales projection; this is below $400 billion and therefore falls in rung 3.\n2026-07-10 v9 10475 3440 1 No FY2027 Data Center consensus or segment guidance is supplied, so there is no direct reference rung. The nearest company reference is $91 billion of total revenue guidance for Q2 FY2027, which is not itself an FY2027 Data Center figure and cannot be assigned a rung on this ladder. About $357 billion for FY2027: apply the Q1 Data Center share of 92% to the $91 billion Q2 total-revenue guide to estimate roughly $83.8 billion of Q2 Data Center revenue, then carry forward the 11.5% sequential growth implied by total-revenue guidance for the remaining quarters.\n2026-07-11 v14 2079 1400 0 Bloomberg-compiled FY2027 sales projection of $393 billion; this market reference sits in rung 3 ($350 billion to less than $400 billion). About $393 billion for FY2027, using Bloomberg's specific projection. The AI-lab demand share and supportive capex and export-policy themes add upside pressure, but state no FY2027 NVIDIA revenue adjustment, so they do not imply a figure above $400 billion.\n2026-07-12 v14 4997 3039 1 Bloomberg's FY2027 sales projection of $393 billion is the specific market reference and sits in rung 3 ($350 billion to less than $400 billion), $7 billion short of rung 2. About $387 billion: starting with Q1 revenue of $81.6 billion and Q2 guidance of approximately $91 billion, I carry the roughly 11.5% sequential increase forward to Q3 and Q4. This remains within rung 3 and below $400 billion.\n2026-07-12 v9 11687 4442 1 No FY2027 Data Center consensus or segment guidance is supplied. The closest company reference is NVIDIA's $91B Q2 FY2027 total-revenue guidance, which, using Q1 Data Center's approximately 92% share and carrying forward the guide-implied sequential growth, corresponds to about $357B for FY2027—rung 3. About $400–410B of FY2027 Data Center revenue. I use the Q1 $75.25B result and Q2 growth outlook as the operating base, then give partial—not full—weight to the roughly $1T Blackwell/Vera Rubin visibility across calendar 2026–27 because it spans multiple periods and products; the discounted estimate is just above the $400B rung boundary.\n2026-07-10 2026-07-12 5 31158 13293 0.058573799999999995\n2026-09-14 v14 22099 3914 1 The latest cited Wall Street estimate is $411 billion (e4061), which sits in rung 2. The updated Zacks consensus growth estimate implies about $404.5 billion from FY2026 revenue, also rung 2. About $407.1 billion: $81.6 billion in Q1, $96.2 billion in Q2, and $108 billion at the Q3 guidance midpoint, plus an estimated $121.3 billion in Q4 by extending the roughly 12.3% Q2-to-Q3 sequential growth rate. This is above $400 billion and below $450 billion.\n2026-09-14 v9 23753 5348 1 The market reference carried from the previous judgement is approximately $372 billion, which sits in rung 3 ($350 billion to below $400 billion). Approximately $414 billion: FY2027 Q1 and Q2 Data Center revenue total about $164.25 billion; the $108 billion Q3 total-revenue guide implies about $100 billion of Data Center revenue at the latest reported mix. Carrying forward the prior H2 baseline of about $208 billion and applying SemiAnalysis’s 20% above-estimates forecast gives about $249.6 billion for H2, including Q3, and about $414 billion for FY2027.\n2026-09-15 v14 19948 4505 1 The market reference is Wall Street's approximately $411 billion FY2027 revenue estimate, in rung 2 ($400 billion to below $450 billion). The Zacks FY2027 growth estimate of 87.4% applied to FY2026 revenue of about $215.9 billion implies approximately $404.5 billion, also rung 2. FY2027 revenue of approximately $418.9 billion: $81.6 billion Q1 plus $96.2 billion Q2, an estimated $113.6 billion Q3 (3.1% above the $110.16 billion high end of guidance), and approximately $127.5 billion Q4 carrying forward the 12.3% sequential growth implied by Q2-to-Q3 guidance.\n2026-09-15 v9 21230 3741 1 Approximately $414 billion is the reference expectation, in rung 2 ($400 billion to below $450 billion). About $379 billion: $75.25 billion in Q1 plus $89.0 billion in Q2, about $100 billion in Q3 (the $108 billion total-revenue guide multiplied by the recent 92.5% Data Center mix), and roughly $115 billion in Q4, allowing for management's stated reacceleration. The total falls in rung 3.\n2026-09-16 v14 18996 3844 0 Wall Street analyst expectations of about $411 billion (e4097, e4348) are in rung 2; Zacks' 87.4% growth estimate implies about $404.5 billion using FY2026 revenue, also rung 2. About $419 billion: reported Q1 and Q2 revenue total $177.8 billion; Q3 is estimated at about $113.6 billion by applying the reported 3.1% average beat to the $110.16 billion high end of guidance, and Q4 at about $127.6 billion by carrying forward approximately 12.3% sequential growth.\n2026-09-16 v9 21475 3953 1 The approximately $414 billion FY2027 expectation carried from the previous conclusion is the reference; it sits at rung 2 ($400 billion to below $450 billion). About $382 billion for FY2027: $75.25 billion in Q1 plus $89 billion in Q2, about $100 billion in Q3 (the $108 billion total-revenue guide at the recent 92.5% Data Center mix), and about $115–120 billion in Q4 by carrying Q3 growth forward with management's stated Q4 hyperscale reacceleration.\n2026-09-17 v14 18478 3814 1 Wall Street analysts expect about $411 billion for FY2027 (rung 2); Zacks’ 87.4% growth estimate implies about $404.5 billion using FY2026 revenue of approximately $215.9 billion (also rung 2). Using Q1 revenue of $81.6 billion and Q2 revenue of $96.2 billion, estimate Q3 at about $113.6 billion by applying the reported 3.1% average beat to the $110.16 billion high end of the $108 billion guidance. Carrying forward the roughly 12.3% sequential growth implied by Q2-to-Q3 guidance gives Q4 of about $127.6 billion, or approximately $419 billion for FY2027.\n2026-09-17 v9 18867 4548 0 Approximately $414 billion is the market expectation, placing the reference at rung 2 ($400 billion to below $450 billion). About $382 billion: Q1 and Q2 total approximately $164.25 billion; applying the recent 92.5% Data Center mix to the $108 billion Q3 total-revenue guide implies about $99.9 billion for Q3; carrying that run rate forward with Q4 hyperscale reacceleration implies roughly $115–120 billion for Q4.\n2026-09-18 v14 19868 5739 1 The latest supplied direct analyst expectation is $411 billion for FY2027, which is rung 2. Zacks' 87.4% growth estimate applied to FY2026 revenue of about $215.9 billion implies roughly $404.5 billion, also rung 2. About $419 billion: Q1 and Q2 reported revenue total $177.8 billion; the $108 billion Q3 guide, adjusted toward the $113–114 billion analyst estimate and the recent 3.1% average beat of guidance's high end, implies roughly $113.6 billion for Q3. Carrying approximately 12% sequential growth into Q4 implies about $127.2 billion, for approximately $418.6 billion across FY2027.\n2026-09-18 v9 22710 3811 1 Market consensus is approximately $414 billion for FY2027, placing the reference at rung 2 ($400 billion to below $450 billion). About $379–384 billion: roughly $164 billion in the first half, about $100 billion in Q3 based on the $108 billion total-revenue guidance and recent Data Center mix, and approximately $115–120 billion in Q4 as hyperscale growth reaccelerates and Rubin supply builds.\n2026-09-19 v14 19168 3550 0 Wall Street analysts expect about $411 billion of FY2027 revenue, placing the reference at rung 2. Zacks' estimate of 87.4% growth applied to FY2026 revenue of about $215.9 billion implies about $405 billion, also rung 2. Approximately $418 billion: $81.6 billion reported in Q1 plus $96.2 billion in Q2, about $113.5 billion estimated for Q3, and about $127 billion for Q4 by carrying roughly 12% sequential growth forward from the estimated Q3 level.\n2026-09-19 v9 20471 3856 1 Approximately $414 billion for FY2027, which sits at rung 2 (Bullish: $400 billion to below $450 billion). About $385–390 billion: approximately $164 billion in Q1–Q2, about $100 billion in Q3 from the $108 billion total-revenue guide and recent Data Center mix, plus roughly $120–125 billion in Q4 as hyperscale growth reaccelerates and Rubin supply builds.\n2026-09-20 v14 17790 4107 1 Market expectation is about $411 billion for FY2027, rung 2 ($400 billion to less than $450 billion). Zacks' 87.4% growth estimate applied to FY2026 revenue of approximately $215.9 billion implies about $405 billion, also rung 2. About $419 billion: Q1 $81.6 billion plus Q2 $96.2 billion, estimated Q3 of about $113.5 billion (the $110.16 billion guidance high end plus the reported average 3.1% beat), and Q4 of about $127 billion by carrying forward the guided 12% sequential growth.\n2026-09-20 v9 18361 7590 1 The market reference supplied by the previous conclusion is approximately $414 billion for FY2027, which sits at rung 2 ($400 billion to below $450 billion). Approximately $410 billion: $164 billion reported in the first half, about $100 billion implied for Q3 from the $108 billion total-revenue guide and recent Data Center mix, and roughly $146 billion estimated for Q4. The Q4 estimate reflects management's expected hyperscale reacceleration and Rubin ramp, with a discounted contribution from SemiAnalysis's forecast that second-half Data Center revenue would exceed analyst estimates by 20%.\n2026-09-14 2026-09-20 14 283214 62320 0.35688840000000005\n2026-09-19 2026-09-20 4 75790 19103 0.102783\nold-1\nv1 ('How much credit support for AI clouds will NVIDIA have committed at the end of FY2027?', 1, 'asset', 'company') [(1, 'Strongly bullish', 0.0, 1000000000.0), (2, 'Bullish', 1000000000.0, 5000000000.0), (3, 'Neutral', 5000000000.0, 10000000000.0), (4, 'Bearish', 10000000000.0, 20000000000.0), (5, 'Strongly bearish', 20000000000.0, None)]\nv4 (\"What will NVIDIA's total revenue be in FY2027?\", 22, 'asset', 'company') [(1, 'Strongly bullish', 431200000000.0, None), (2, 'Bullish', 392000000000.0, 431200000000.0), (3, 'Neutral', 352800000000.0, 392000000000.0), (4, 'Bearish', 313600000000.0, 352800000000.0), (5, 'Strongly bearish', None, 313600000000.0)]\nv8 ('How much Data Center segment revenue will NVIDIA report for FY2027?', 62, 'asset', 'company') [(1, 'Strongly bullish', 400000000000.0, None), (2, 'Bullish', 350000000000.0, 400000000000.0), (3, 'Neutral', 300000000000.0, 350000000000.0), (4, 'Bearish', 250000000000.0, 300000000000.0), (5, 'Strongly bearish', None, 250000000000.0)]\n('2026-08-02', 'No aggregate market consensus or NVIDIA guidance is supplied, so there is no external reference figure to place on the ladder. The carried base case of roughly $10–11 billion is in rung 4.', 'More than $20 billion committed by FY2027 is the most likely outcome: carrying forward the roughly $10–11 billion base and assigning only about 4% of the reported $250 billion OpenAI guarantee headline—about $10 billion—as the incremental expected contribution yields roughly $20–21 billion. This discounts the headline for the ongoing, changeable negotiations rather than counting the full $250 billion.')\n('2026-08-03', 'No aggregate market consensus or NVIDIA guidance for total FY2027 credit-support obligations is supplied. The carried base estimate of about $10–11 billion is the available reference and sits in rung 4; the reported $250 billion Ohio proposal is not itself an established reference for committed obligations.', 'About $20–21 billion by FY2027 year-end: carry forward the roughly $10–11 billion base estimate and add an estimated roughly $10 billion for the Ohio backstop, heavily discounted from the reported $250 billion proposal because negotiations remain ongoing and the amount and timing of the reported announcement are unspecified.')\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/extraction.py | sed -n '402,450p'\nnl -ba src/hivemind/views/writing.py | sed -n '72,81p;175,205p;223,266p'\nnl -ba docs/research/2026-10-26-theme-dependencies/design.md | sed -n '73,91p;176,185p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/extraction.py | sed -n '402,450p'\nnl -ba src/hivemind/views/writing.py | sed -n '72,81p;175,205p;223,266p'\nnl -ba docs/research/2026-10-26-theme-dependencies/design.md | sed -n '73,91p;176,185p'\"","aggregated_output":"   402\t    parts.append(item_header(item, category) + text[:MAX_TEXT_CHARS])\n   403\t    parts.append(CLOSING)\n   404\t    parts.append(_read(f'review-{version}.txt').strip())\n   405\t    return _read(f'role-{version}.txt'), '\\n\\n'.join(parts)\n   406\t\n   407\t\n   408\tOBJECT_LABELS = vocabulary.ASSET_LABELS\n   409\t\n   410\t\n   411\tdef check_ladder(rungs, kind):\n   412\t    \"\"\"None when the ladder is well formed, else the problem. An asset ladder written from Strongly bearish up to\n   413\t    Strongly bullish (the model often orders a revenue ladder by rising value) is the same ladder; normalise_ladder\n   414\t    turns it round. Labels are compared in the canonical vocabulary.\"\"\"\n   415\t    if len(rungs) not in (2, 5):\n   416\t        return f'ladder has {len(rungs)} rungs, needs 5 (or 2 for yes/no)'\n   417\t    if any(not r['label'].strip() or not r['condition'].strip() for r in rungs):\n   418\t        return 'a rung has an empty label or condition'\n   419\t    if kind == 'asset' and len(rungs) == 5:\n   420\t        labels = [vocabulary.canonical('label', r['label']) for r in rungs]\n   421\t        if labels != OBJECT_LABELS and labels != OBJECT_LABELS[::-1]:\n   422\t            return f'object view rungs must be {OBJECT_LABELS}, got {labels}'\n   423\t    return None\n   424\t\n   425\t\n   426\tdef normalise_ladder(rungs, kind):\n   427\t    \"\"\"Position 1 is Strongly bullish (06-views): a reversed asset ladder is turned round, label and condition together.\"\"\"\n   428\t    if kind == 'asset' and len(rungs) == 5 and [vocabulary.canonical('label', r['label']) for r in rungs] == OBJECT_LABELS[::-1]:\n   429\t        return list(reversed(rungs))\n   430\t    return rungs\n   431\t\n   432\t\n   433\t# 06-views ladder rule 6: a quarterly or half-year figure is evidence, not a view. The half-year forms name a revenue\n   434\t# or sales figure (H1 收入, first-half revenue); an event scheduled in a half-year (ships in H2 2026) is not a figure.\n   435\tQUARTERLY = re.compile(r'(\\bQ[1-4]\\b|第[一二三四1-4]季|季度|\\bquarter(?!ly report)|fiscal Q[1-4]|\\b(?:[12]H|H[12])\\b(?:\\s+(?:FY)?\\d{4})?\\s*收入|上半年收入|下半年收入'\n   436\t                       r'|\\b(?:[12]H|H[12])\\b(?:\\s+(?:FY)?\\d{4})?\\s+(?:revenue|sales|net sales)|\\b(?:first|second)[- ]half(?:[- ]year)?\\s+(?:revenue|sales|net sales)'\n   437\t                       r'|\\bhalf[- ]year\\s+(?:revenue|sales|net sales))', re.I)\n   438\t\n   439\t\n   440\tdef request_for(cfg, item, text, shown_views, universe):\n   441\t    \"\"\"Build the setting, complete prompt and schema without making a call.\"\"\"\n   442\t    setting = cfg.extraction_setting(item['category'])\n   443\t    version = setting.prompt_version.rpartition('-')[2]\n   444\t    system, user = build_prompt(item, text, shown_views, universe, version)\n   445\t    return setting, system, user, schema_for(version)\n   446\t\n   447\t\n   448\t@dataclasses.dataclass\n   449\tclass Reading:\n   450\t    \"\"\"An item read: the extraction answer through the code checks, before the handover (the parallel day prepares it early and\n    72\tdef oriented_like(c, previous, notes):\n    73\t    \"\"\"06-views: a successor's ladder keeps the predecessor's direction. A numeric ladder written the other way round (rung 1 the\n    74\t    lowest band where the predecessor's rung 1 is the highest) is the same ladder; it is stored reversed, rungs with their\n    75\t    labels and bounds, so positions mean the same along the chain. Undecidable pairs are stored as written.\"\"\"\n    76\t    from .matching import ladder_direction\n    77\t    before, after = (ladder_direction(previous) if previous else None), ladder_direction(c['rungs'])\n    78\t    if before is not None and after is not None and before != after:\n    79\t        notes.append(f'candidate {c[\"id\"]}: successor ladder reversed to the predecessor\\'s direction')\n    80\t        return dict(c, rungs=list(reversed(c['rungs'])))\n    81\t    return c\n   175\t    # 2. dependencies of the new views (candidate ids resolve to the views just created)\n   176\t    dependencies_written = set()\n   177\t    for c in order:\n   178\t        outcome, target, deps = checked.outcomes.get(c['id'], ('skip', None, []))\n   179\t        if c['id'] not in new_views:\n   180\t            continue\n   181\t        view_id = new_views[c['id']]\n   182\t        for dep in deps:\n   183\t            depends_on = dep['view_id']\n   184\t            if depends_on in new_views:\n   185\t                depends_on = new_views[depends_on]\n   186\t            elif depends_on in candidate_ids:\n   187\t                notes.append(f'dependency {view_id} -> candidate {depends_on} dropped: that candidate was not opened')\n   188\t                continue\n   189\t            if depends_on and store.would_cycle(conn, view_id, depends_on):\n   190\t                notes.append(f'dependency {view_id} -> {depends_on} dropped: cycle')\n   191\t                continue\n   192\t            chain = dep['wait_chain_view_id']\n   193\t            if chain in new_views:\n   194\t                chain = new_views[chain]\n   195\t            wait_year = dep['wait_year']\n   196\t            if wait_year and chain and hasattr(universe, 'canonical_year'):          # the chain's object decides the spelling (FY2027 or 2026)\n   197\t                chain_view = store.view(conn, chain)\n   198\t                wait_year = universe.canonical_year(chain_view['object_id'] if chain_view else object_id_of(universe, c), wait_year)\n   199\t            edge = (view_id, depends_on, chain, wait_year, dep['direction'])\n   200\t            if edge in dependencies_written:\n   201\t                continue\n   202\t            dependencies_written.add(edge)\n   203\t            store.insert(conn, 'dependencies', view_id=view_id, depends_on=depends_on, wait_chain_view_id=chain, wait_year=wait_year,\n   204\t                         direction=dep['direction'], seq=seq)\n   205\t        resolve_waiting(conn, view_id, seq, changed)\n   223\t        targets = destinations(e)\n   224\t        if not targets:\n   225\t            notes.append(f'evidence {e[\"id\"]} linked to nothing kept; not stored')\n   226\t            continue\n   227\t        # one piece is stored once however many views it goes to (06-views: 一条证据连几条观点，也只存一条); a repeat\n   228\t        # under any destination stores the piece and relates it to the old one (D204), a replacement under any\n   229\t        # destination records a revision there and links everywhere, a late older statement is logged and stored as new (D202)\n   230\t        repeat_of = next((target for _, (outcome, target, _) in targets if outcome == 'repeat' and target), None)\n   231\t        replacing = [(target, said_day) for _, (outcome, target, said_day) in targets if outcome == 'replace' and target]\n   232\t        if repeat_of:\n   233\t            # D204: the piece is stored as its own record with its own links; the matcher's \"same claim\" is a relation, not a merge\n   234\t            stored_id = _store_piece(conn, e, seq, item)\n   235\t            store.relate_same(conn, repeat_of, stored_id, seq)\n   236\t            for view_id, _ in targets:\n   237\t                store.link(conn, stored_id, view_id, seq)\n   238\t                changed.add(view_id)\n   239\t            evidence_ids[e['id']] = stored_id\n   240\t            continue\n   241\t        if replacing:\n   242\t            target_id, said_day = replacing[0]\n   243\t            old = store.evidence(conn, target_id)\n   244\t            new_day = said_day or e['original_day'] or item['publication_day']\n   245\t            if old and old['original_day'] and new_day < old['original_day']:\n   246\t                # D202: an older statement arriving late is one more piece in force (before, it was logged and linked nowhere)\n   247\t                store.insert(conn, 'late_statements', input_id=item['input_id'], evidence_quote=e['quote'][:500], reason=f'older than {target_id} ({old[\"original_day\"]})', seq=seq)\n   248\t                notes.append(f'evidence {e[\"id\"]}: older than {target_id} ({old[\"original_day\"]}); stored as new, no revision')\n   249\t                replacing = []\n   250\t            refusal = revision_refused(e, old, new_day) if replacing else ''\n   251\t            if refusal:\n   252\t                # 06-views: a revision is a later account of the same matter by a party entitled to give one; anything else is one more piece\n   253\t                notes.append(f'evidence {e[\"id\"]}: revision of {target_id} refused ({refusal}); stored as new')\n   254\t                replacing = []\n   255\t        if replacing:\n   256\t            stored_id = _store_piece(conn, e, seq, item)                     # D203: the stated day is stored; new_day orders the revision only\n   257\t            for target_id, _ in replacing:\n   258\t                store.revise(conn, target_id, stored_id, new_day, seq)          # D202: both pieces stay in force\n   259\t                for linked in store.views_linked_to(conn, target_id):\n   260\t                    if store.link(conn, stored_id, linked, seq) and store.is_open(conn, linked):\n   261\t                        changed.add(linked)\n   262\t            for view_id, _ in targets:\n   263\t                store.link(conn, stored_id, view_id, seq)\n   264\t                changed.add(view_id)\n   265\t            evidence_ids[e['id']] = stored_id\n   266\t            continue\n    73\t### 3. How later items add links\n    74\t\n    75\t- A later company item whose model reads a theme in its shown list (block 5 shows the theme theses linked to the\n    76\t  item's objects today only through dependencies; it must also show the open theme theses of themes the item is\n    77\t  tagged with, which classification already supplies as object identifiers) may answer `feeds` on an *existing*\n    78\t  company thesis: `{target: v30, depends_on: v12, direction, why}`. This needs one change the PRD does not allow today:\n    79\t  \"choose dependencies only when B is created\" becomes \"when B is created or when an item first shows the mechanism\";\n    80\t  the writer adds the dependency with its sequence number, append-only, and rejudges B.\n    81\t- A correction (an item shows the opposite sign) appends a new dependency record and marks the old one superseded\n    82\t  (same shape as evidence replacement); history keeps both.\n    83\t- A second company reading the same theme adds its own link with its own sign; nothing is copied across companies.\n    84\t\n    85\t### 4. The admission reasons, amended\n    86\t\n    87\t- `policy_stage`: a stage of a policy process, decided by a named authority, **whose outcome moves a company line the\n    88\t  candidate names**. A proceeding with no such line is evidence or nothing.\n    89\t- `industry_aggregate` becomes `shared_quantity`: a quantity or price outside any one company that several companies\n    90\t  move on (an industry aggregate, an oil price, a policy rate, an exchange rate), one per calendar year, **with the\n    91\t  company lines it moves named**. This absorbs Codex's proposed `macro_condition` without a fifth category: oil and the\n   176\t\n   177\t## Decisions for Alex\n   178\t\n   179\t1. Rename `industry_aggregate` to `shared_quantity` and require `feeds` on theme candidates (this document §1, §4).\n   180\t2. Allow a dependency to be added to an existing thesis by a later item (changes 06-views \"only when B is created\").\n   181\t3. The cold case: a theme from a macro-only item opens only when the theme is in the universe's list; otherwise refused.\n   182\t4. Composition (component ↔ aggregate) stays evidence, not dependency, as the PRD has it.\n   183\t\n   184\t## 7. The decided shape: one theme, every company; the sign decided at judgement\n   185\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c '\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport sqlite3,json,re\nroot=Path(\\\"poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/prod\\\")\ndef db(p):\n return sqlite3.connect(p.resolve().as_uri()+\\\"?mode=ro&immutable=1\\\",uri=True)\nwith db(root/\\\"views.sqlite\\\") as c, db(root/\\\"archive.sqlite\\\") as a:\n for v in (\\\"v9\\\",\\\"v14\\\"):\n  print(\\\"number evidence links\\\",v,c.execute(\\\"select count(distinct evidence_id) from evidence_links where view_id=?\\\",(v,)).fetchone()[0])\n  for day,call,ref in c.execute(\\\"select publication_day,call_id,reference from judgements where view_id=? and publication_day between '\\\\''2026-07-10'\\\\'' and '\\\\''2026-07-12'\\\\'' order by judgement_id\\\",(v,)):\n   req=json.loads(a.execute(\\\"select request_json from model_calls where call_id=?\\\",(call,)).fetchone()[0])[\\\"messages\\\"][-1][\\\"content\\\"]\n   print(day,v,\\\"393?\\\",bool(re.search(r'\\\\''\\\\b393\\\\b'\\\\'',req)),\\\"e195?\\\",'\\\\''e195'\\\\'' in req,\\\"81.6?\\\",'\\\\''81.6'\\\\'' in req,\\\"75.25?\\\",'\\\\''75.25'\\\\'' in req,\\\"\"'$91?\",'\"'\\\\''\"'$91'\"'\\\\'' in req)\n print(\\\"find evidence detail\\\",c.execute(\\\"select evidence_id,quote from evidence where evidence_id in ('\\\\''e195'\\\\'','\\\\''e204'\\\\'','\\\\''e238'\\\\'','\\\\''e240'\\\\'')\\\").fetchall())\n'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 -c '\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport sqlite3,json,re\nroot=Path(\\\"poc/data/comparison-2026-11-17/run/old-2/prod\\\")\ndef db(p):\n return sqlite3.connect(p.resolve().as_uri()+\\\"?mode=ro&immutable=1\\\",uri=True)\nwith db(root/\\\"views.sqlite\\\") as c, db(root/\\\"archive.sqlite\\\") as a:\n for v in (\\\"v9\\\",\\\"v14\\\"):\n  print(\\\"number evidence links\\\",v,c.execute(\\\"select count(distinct evidence_id) from evidence_links where view_id=?\\\",(v,)).fetchone()[0])\n  for day,call,ref in c.execute(\\\"select publication_day,call_id,reference from judgements where view_id=? and publication_day between '\\\\''2026-07-10'\\\\'' and '\\\\''2026-07-12'\\\\'' order by judgement_id\\\",(v,)):\n   req=json.loads(a.execute(\\\"select request_json from model_calls where call_id=?\\\",(call,)).fetchone()[0])[\\\"messages\\\"][-1][\\\"content\\\"]\n   print(day,v,\\\"393?\\\",bool(re.search(r'\\\\''\\\\b393\\\\b'\\\\'',req)),\\\"e195?\\\",'\\\\''e195'\\\\'' in req,\\\"81.6?\\\",'\\\\''81.6'\\\\'' in req,\\\"75.25?\\\",'\\\\''75.25'\\\\'' in req,\\\"\"'$91?\",'\"'\\\\''\"'$91'\"'\\\\'' in req)\n print(\\\"find evidence detail\\\",c.execute(\\\"select evidence_id,quote from evidence where evidence_id in ('\\\\''e195'\\\\'','\\\\''e204'\\\\'','\\\\''e238'\\\\'','\\\\''e240'\\\\'')\\\").fetchall())\n'\"","aggregated_output":"number evidence links v9 1287\n2026-07-10 v9 393? False e195? False 81.6? True 75.25? True $91? True\n2026-07-12 v9 393? False e195? False 81.6? True 75.25? True $91? True\nnumber evidence links v14 1329\n2026-07-10 v14 393? True e195? True 81.6? False 75.25? False $91? False\n2026-07-11 v14 393? True e195? True 81.6? False 75.25? False $91? False\n2026-07-12 v14 393? True e195? True 81.6? True 75.25? False $91? True\nfind evidence detail [('e195', 'The chipmaker is projected to deliver $228 billion in profits on sales of $393 billion in fiscal 2027, which ends Jan. 31. That would represent an expansion of 90% and 82%, respectively, according to data compiled by Bloomberg.'), ('e204', 'The company reported record revenue of $81.6 billion, up 85% year over year and 20% sequentially, with Data Center revenue reaching $75.2 billion.'), ('e238', 'For the first quarter of fiscal 2027, revenue jumped 85% year-over-year (YOY) to $81.6 billion, easily beating analyst expectations.'), ('e240', 'Management also issued strong guidance, forecasting approximately $91 billion in Q2 revenue despite assuming no China data-center sales because of export restrictions.')]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
