{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-10-26-theme-dependencies/design.md | sed -n '12,59p;174,223p'\nrg -n -i 'composition|component.*aggregate|aggregate.*component|component cannot exceed|part reading its whole' docs/DECISIONS-log.md docs/DECISIONS.md docs/prd/06-views.md | head -75\nrg -n '\"'^## D(186|258) '\"' docs/DECISIONS-log.md\"","aggregated_output":"    12\t\n    13\t| Piece | Where | Status on the r3 ledger |\n    14\t|---|---|---|\n    15\t| Theme thesis: a question about the world with an outcome ladder, no good/bad label | 06-views \"Two thesis kinds\" | 16 theme theses (9 export-control stages, 7 aggregates) |\n    16\t| Dependency: thesis B reads thesis A's conclusion, with a direction per dependant (rate cuts: bullish for Ethereum, bearish for JPM) | 06-views dependency tree and rules | 0 rows, ever: the Jev matcher writes `dependencies: []` for every candidate (`jev_matching.py` line 249) and the extractor is never asked |\n    17\t| Awaited dependency: B depends on A's next-period thesis that does not exist yet; bind when created | 06-views dependencies, `store.dependencies` (`wait_chain_view_id`, `wait_year`) | 0 rows |\n    18\t| Research group: the folder for one continuing matter across companies and themes | 06-views research groups (D149) | 24 groups, 38 memberships |\n    19\t| Rejudging propagates a changed conclusion to dependants | 06-views state rules | never exercised |\n    20\t\n    21\tSo the design exists; the part that makes a theme worth holding (its links) has no producer. Everything below is about\n    22\tproducing and checking links, not about new concepts.\n    23\t\n    24\t## How a senior analyst holds a theme (the brain to copy)\n    25\t\n    26\t- The unit is a dated, falsifiable question about the world with a few outcomes: \"where is the Fed's upper bound after\n    27\t  the December meeting\", \"does Commerce license H200 sales to China this year\", \"what do the five hyperscalers spend in\n    28\t  2026\". A regime name (\"Middle East tension\") is a folder, not a question; a scenario (\"supply restored / partly / cut off\")\n    29\t  is a rung.\n    30\t- A theme earns its place by the lines it moves. The analyst writes the chain explicitly: theme outcome → company line\n    31\t  → sign. Oil up: producers' revenue up, airlines' fuel cost up. Same theme, two signs, each stated at the company.\n    32\t- Few at a time: three to five live themes per desk, rotating. The count is an outcome of the test \"does any name I\n    33\t  hold move on this\", never a cap.\n    34\t- Links are added when the company is read, not when the theme is. The theme can be written first (from a macro\n    35\t  document); the link appears the day a company document shows the mechanism.\n    36\t- A proceeding (a prosecutor's charging decision) is not a theme unless it changes a line (market access, supply, a\n    37\t  cash obligation). It can be evidence to a thesis that exists.\n    38\t\n    39\t## The design\n    40\t\n    41\t### 1. What a theme candidate must state\n    42\t\n    43\tA theme candidate (`kind = theme`, reason `policy_stage` or `shared_quantity`, see §4) carries, beside the fields of D184:\n    44\t\n    45\t```\n    46\tfeeds: [ {target: <shown asset thesis id | this answer's candidate id | typed target>, direction: <see below>, why: <one sentence, source-grounded>} ]\n    47\ttyped target = {object: <ticker in the universe>, measure: <vocabulary>, scope: <text>}   # for a company thesis that does not exist yet\n    48\t```\n    49\t\n    50\t- `direction` for an asset dependant: which end of the theme ladder is favourable for the company line (`first_end`,\n    51\t  `last_end`), as the PRD's dependency rules already define; for a theme dependant: `same` or `opposite` orientation.\n    52\t- At least one entry is required for a theme candidate (schema `minItems`-equivalent enforced in `sift`); a company\n    53\t  candidate may carry `feeds` too (a company thesis that depends on a theme), optional.\n    54\t- A typed target (no id) is allowed only from an item that shows no thesis of that company: the extractor names the\n    55\t  line it would move; the writer records the dependency as awaited by key (object, measure, scope), the same table and\n    56\t  mechanism as the awaited chain/year of today, and binds it when a thesis with that key opens (the writer checks at\n    57\t  every write, as it checks awaited years today).\n    58\t\n    59\t### 2. When a theme thesis opens\n   174\t- On the r3 ledger: how many company theses would have gained a link (the 9 export-control and 7 aggregate theses against\n   175\t  the 23 NVDA theses) by the eight rules, read by hand; that is the gold for the first run.\n   176\t\n   177\t## Decisions for Alex\n   178\t\n   179\t1. Rename `industry_aggregate` to `shared_quantity` and require `feeds` on theme candidates (this document §1, §4).\n   180\t2. Allow a dependency to be added to an existing thesis by a later item (changes 06-views \"only when B is created\").\n   181\t3. The cold case: a theme from a macro-only item opens only when the theme is in the universe's list; otherwise refused.\n   182\t4. Composition (component ↔ aggregate) stays evidence, not dependency, as the PRD has it.\n   183\t\n   184\t## 7. The decided shape: one theme, every company; the sign decided at judgement\n   185\t\n   186\t- A theme thesis opens on its own admission test (D184 `policy_stage` / `shared_quantity`: a stage or quantity outside any one\n   187\t  company that several companies move on, with the authority or the settling figure named); from a macro-only item only when\n   188\t  the theme is in the universe's list (point 3). No edge is written at extraction for themes.\n   189\t- Every company thesis is judged with the open theme theses of its themes in view: the judging request gains a block \"Themes in\n   190\t  force\" listing, for each open theme thesis of a theme the company's items were tagged with, its question, current rung and\n   191\t  the reasons of its last judgement. The judge states, per theme it uses, the sign it applies to this company (\"licences\n   192\t  granted: favourable for China revenue\") in the judgement's reasons; code checks that a cited theme is open and tagged, as it\n   193\t  checks cited evidence today. This is the \"别的方法\": the sign lives in the company judgement, where the analyst decides it,\n   194\t  not in a table written in advance.\n   195\t- Propagation: a theme's changed conclusion is not fanned out to every company thesis in the same round (06-views: a repeated\n   196\t  Fed statement must not trigger hundreds of dependants); each company thesis reads the current theme states at its next\n   197\t  judgement, which its own evidence triggers. A theme whose state changed with no company item that day is caught by the daily\n   198\t  judging round of its tagged companies' open theses (D63), bounded by the count of open theses, not of edges.\n   199\t- Explicit dependencies remain for what a document states (a company thesis that reads another thesis's conclusion), may be\n   200\t  added later (point 2), and keep the cycle check.\n   201\t- Research groups keep organising; the admission test keeps proceedings out (a prosecutor's charging decision names no stage\n   202\t  of a policy that several companies move on).\n   203\t- Value × reader change: judging's request builder (new block), judging's answer check (cited themes), the UI (a company card\n   204\t  can show the themes in force), the idea route (themes as context). The dependencies table is unchanged.\n   205\t- What to measure first, at no cost: on the r3 ledger, for each of the 23 NVDA theses, list the open theme theses tagged to\n   206\t  its items on each judgement day and the count of judgements that would have carried a theme block (today 185 judgements,\n   207\t  0 with a theme in view); then re-send three judgements with the block and read whether the sign is stated and right.\n   208\t\n   209\t## 8. Build design for the decided shape (2026-10-26, evening; AGENTS §2 tables; revised after the Codex review, 8.8)\n   210\t\n   211\tAlex: \"做，先零成本数完再改；然后你得确认这个架构和逻辑是对的\". §§1–6 and their tables describe the withdrawn `feeds` shape and\n   212\tstay as the record of what was rejected; this section is the design the build follows. One word: a **theme block** is the\n   213\tpart of a judging request that lists the open theme theses and their current conclusions.\n   214\t\n   215\t### 8.1 What the stored ledgers say ($0, `theme_block_census.py`)\n   216\t\n   217\t| | r3 (`poc-v25`) | r4 (`poc-v26`, the default) |\n   218\t|---|---|---|\n   219\t| judgements: company / theme | 162 / 23 | 175 / 11 |\n   220\t| open theme theses in the window | 16 | 6 |\n   221\t| company judgements that would carry a theme block, one to all | 162 of 162 | 175 of 175 |\n   222\t| theme lines per block (min / median / max) | 1 / 11 / 16 | 2 / 3 / 6 |\n   223\t| company judgements with a theme tagged on the items behind its evidence (the narrow reading) | 12 | 14 |\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2050:- Alex asked to match the Thesis header, remove the redundant decomposition list, and explain/fix why every thesis was drawn after the first. The stored response has three analysis parts, eight distinct chosen theses and five related theses. Its third part maps to none. Across the three stored response fixtures, one has this graph and two have no chosen theses. The FE made the first chosen thesis the parent of the other seven and all five related theses; four of the five related paths ignored their actual `via` source. The backend already supplies each related source, so no backend or model change is needed.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2051:- The Idea and Thesis use one header renderer and a non-shrinking 40px header. Remove the decomposition rows and their IDs from the Idea card; keep its question, verdict and reading. `reading.parts` stays in the response for analysis, not as card rows.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3512:- Result: the D336 UI test fails on the old composition (\"No No restriction adopted\"); 58 UI tests, lint, format and the 20 standing UI mutation checks pass. In headless Chrome, with the cache disabled, v49 shows \"No restriction adopted\" and v14 \"Yes\".\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:6496:  council's review: the four tables of AGENTS §2, covering seed edges and matcher-chosen dependencies (a part reading its whole;\n2476:## D186 · 2026-10-26 · Asset-thesis rungs describe business outcomes; the favourable end is registered per thesis\n3030:## D258 · 2026-11-02 · Question identity brought in line with D248: a part of an open question is filed under it; `event` and `policy_event` are one family and a process's step words are one process; the collision judge is given D248's test\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -i 'component(s)? (is|are|as|of|that)|component.*evidence|aggregation|part.of|分项|组成' docs/prd/06-views.md docs/DECISIONS-log.md | head -70\nnl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '2476,2501p'\nnl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-probe/claude-marks.md | sed -n '12,30p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n -i 'component(s)? (is|are|as|of|that)|component.*evidence|aggregation|part.of|分项|组成' docs/prd/06-views.md docs/DECISIONS-log.md | head -70\nnl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '2476,2501p'\nnl -ba docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-probe/claude-marks.md | sed -n '12,30p'\"","aggregated_output":"docs/prd/06-views.md:78:3. One ladder concerns one thing. Separate numeric and event questions and connect them with dependencies. Likewise, separate components that can move in opposite directions, such as H20 and Blackwell chip classes.\ndocs/prd/06-views.md:180:| Merge into existing | The candidate concerns the same focus or a part of it, such as H20 China revenue within China revenue. Merge only into open theses; closed theses can only be succeeded. | Compare its evidence within the target thesis and preserve grouping under this section's rules. Use the existing ladder and due date. |\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:41:- Decides: the limits section (budget per policy, total budget, concurrency) is not part of Config. Where limits live,\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:68:- Changed by D7: replay is not part of the system design.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:166:  theme part of the universe, not a separate list. Rates, FX and indices are not objects of their own; they are data\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:443:- Decides: financial reports are not part of the stream. When a thesis's ladder or evidence needs a number from a\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:615:- Changed by D51: consensus is not part of the design at all; third-party views stay evidence of their tier.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:836:  call without the document decides, for each candidate, attach to #k (the same thing or a part of it), succeed #k,\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:862:- Changed by D44: no key is matched by code. Whether a candidate is an open view, a part of it or its next period is\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:866:  new view (no match, or only a weak one, is new). How the list is made, the year filter, the outcomes \"part of an open\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:1013:- Decides: whether a candidate view is an open view, a part of it or its next period is decided only by the model in\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:1044:  counted, with a code filter; how the list is made and a theme view's identity; the outcomes \"part of an open view\"\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:1093:  6. A candidate that is a part of an open view goes into that view (\"H20 in China\" into \"China revenue\"). Alex: \"行\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:1282:  3. Consensus is not part of the design: a view has one state, judged by the model from its evidence whenever that\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:1286:     questions per object is part of it); the labelling details (with how to check evidence that extraction attached\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:1422:     them as a whole. Freezing the views due that day is part of that run. Nothing waits for the day's items.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:1462:     status line), name every part of the old draft no longer used, adding the 7-day backstop for a weakened premise\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2092:- The isolated POC uses three original articles, three independent samples and ordinary-ingestion controls. New grouping fields are part of existing extraction/matching calls; original checks and writer are reused. No sealed database, production prompt, MCP or UI changes.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2173:- Alex asks to refresh the relevant PRDs so group association is implicitly needed during extraction. Organization is part of reading incoming information, not an optional later whole-library clustering step. Every proposed thesis carries structured membership in a continuing business subject; evidence-only updates follow the existing thesis memberships.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2250:- Alex 看过验收审查后要求「好你开始吧，我们一起看」。先修验收定义和离线检查入口，用已存结果及受控反例验证，不把旧关系保留或零次判断报成新归组成功。\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2282:- 最小下一步见 `docs/research/2026-10-25-extraction-continuity.md`：三个真实 Ohio 输入、两臂各三次连续样本，两臂都沿用已有组成员上下文、身份与原子保存，仅改变实验角色的阅读入口。默认角色和归组仍不改变；本轮不声称验证大库检索。\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2424:- The only runtime state restored is the assistant-set semantic `settings.halted` flag in the isolated study budget journal. A backup precedes the update; all 12 completed attempts, charges and the original limits are unchanged. No unknown-usage or technical-failure state is reopened. The next trial is concurrent-1; no paid request is part of this rollback.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2462:- Code review before the push ([request](research/2026-10-26-e2e-parallel/review-2-request.txt), [Codex, read-only](research/2026-10-26-e2e-parallel/review-2.txt); no correctness defect in request identity, commit order, matching order or thread ownership). Fixed, each with a test that failed first: (1) a restart under `--max-items-per-day` counted only the remaining items, so it dispatched an item beyond the day's limit (serial) or was refused by the manifest (parallel); the items an earlier run of the day wrote now count toward the limit. (2) The study and test comparison read 12 of the ledger's 20 tables; one comparison (`proof.ledger_rows`) now reads every product table without row ids, call ids and wall-clock times, and recomparing every stored pair found them identical (D180's recorded day, the 16-worker recorded run, the product-entry live run, the six D181 cross-replays, D182's fifteen days: 5,805 rows), the D182 mutant differing in 16 tables. (3) The entry point is tested with no arguments on the default Jev configuration (16 and 8 workers, serial ledger; a mutant default is caught). (4) A stale sentence in the current state. Found by Claude: a manifest left by another ledger in the same folder refused a fresh ledger that had written nothing of that day; such a manifest is now replaced, and a ledger that has written part of the day still refuses a changed contract.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2496:- Review of Jev's relation criteria against the r3 ledger ([probe](../poc/reports/2026-10-26-admission-v12/jev-relation-probe/probe.md), 31 stored candidate calls whose list holds a thesis of the same object and measure, 18 labelled by the assistant): under the current options Jev calls a population variant of one aggregate `part_of` (0.4–0.9) and the code maps that to \"new\"; under an analyst's option set (\"one question: the same outcome settles both; another estimate, population or proxy of one aggregate is the same question\") it answers `distinct_question_same_matter` 0.5–0.9 on the same pairs. Both wordings: 8 of 18 right. Jev compares wording; it does not hold the decision. No change to Jev's criteria is made: the measured criteria stay (D167–D169).\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2699:  duplicates by wording (the collision judge's `distinct_question_same_matter` on `same_quantity_or_event`/`part_of` pairs) and 1 a\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2767:- Preserve V4 and its read results. Reassess the same 48 saved answers with V5; the source-venue-only penalty on Luna/revenue-clean-3/G09 is removed, while its time-field problem remains. This changes evaluation, not product behaviour or model capability. No new product call, default promotion or full-pipeline run is part of this standards correction.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2831:- Measurement, in this order: the per-article reference for the v38 week's 98 items and the 20-article holdout of 2026-07-08..14 (`holdout-pick.json`) written from the texts and frozen before any send; three gpt-6-luna draws of the production bytes and three Haiku 5.5 draws of the same text and schema (`haiku_week.py`, expected $0.78); every answer through the production sift; scored by the standard's §11 (structure by code, content by reading, core and supporting apart, no composite). role-v23 (the three conflicts in gold-check.md §5) is the arm after the measurement, not part of it.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2918:- Decided (the work, not its content): prompt changes and sends stop; a unified standard draft (`docs/research/2026-10-29-ledger-standard/standard-v2*.md`) merges the signed standard (D229) with the recorded decisions and PRD 06, is checked by independent readers on fixed cases over several rounds and by a read-only drift review against the decisions, and goes to Alex for review with every behaviour change listed for his decision; a golden set traced to the article text and to the standard's sentences is built from it as the test standard for prompt changes. Until Alex signs, the signed standard (D229) stays the ruler and no part of the draft is adopted.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:2985:- The ruler (Alex: \"你要修正尺子\"): the standard page goes to version 5 with these rules, then a read-only drift review; the gold's evidence part is re-derived for version 5 (version 4 changed no evidence entry, `gold-v4-evidence-check.md`) by two independent readers with every disagreement decided against the article, written as a new frozen file with every change listed (before, after, reason), the version-3 file untouched (D243 item 11); the opening part of the gold is not re-derived here and the scorer reports no question score until it is. The scorer refuses a gold whose evidence part was made for another version of the page: `final_scores.py` had bypassed `score_gold.py`'s version check and scored rounds since D248 on the version-3 gold, which is the false measurement Alex names.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3030:## D258 · 2026-11-02 · Question identity brought in line with D248: a part of an open question is filed under it; `event` and `policy_event` are one family and a process's step words are one process; the collision judge is given D248's test\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3032:- Alex, 2026-11-02 00:05, on why questions were duplicated although the matching step sees every open question: \"开题为什么重复？你不是都可以看到存在的题了吗那你操他妈的在干嘛你到底系统有没有接对\"; then \"我刚才说的这个问题你也发现是什么 part of 问题你不该去反思一下这个设计或是哪里有问题直接修直接改。开干。用这个思路来一个一个的提升我们的能力。不要陷入无限没必要的测试循环\".\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3033:- The wiring is as designed (every candidate is compared with every open question by Jev, and the collision judge is asked); the duplicates come from the identity rules, which predate D248. Census of the 23 questions one draw's articles opened (arm 3 d1, `research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/review-2026-11-02.md`; the three draws in `replay-part-of-r3.txt`): 10 were ones Jev had called `part_of` an open question (ZTE's H200 licence of the China authorization question, the CoreWeave backstop and the credit-support programme of the financing-commitments total, Rubin shipping by September of Rubin launching by December), and `part_of` fell through to \"new question\"; 5 were deadline variants or a launch beside a shipment (R2-a/b, built 2026-10-31, measured only tonight as arm 4); 1 opened because the model typed the China H200 authorization as `event` against the seed's `policy_event` and two more because its event-type word for the one licensing process varied (licence, approval, other), each a typed-field conflict that blocked a Jev \"same\" of 0.85–0.92 before the judge was ever asked; 3 are the GAAP/non-GAAP and growth/level variants (R2-d, open); 4 were new matters.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3035:  - R2-e: a candidate Jev calls `part_of` an open question (above the threshold) is filed under that question, like a `same_quantity_or_event` verdict, when the typed fields allow; the part is evidence of the card, not a card of its own. The typed fields still decide: a yes/no signing question never merges into an amount question (D248 item 1's recorded exception, the Ohio lease guarantee) because `event` and `financing_amount` conflict. The collision judge is consulted as before and may keep a component apart under its rule.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3037:  - The collision judge's prompt gains D248's test (`collision-v2.txt`): a single deal, counterparty or instance under a plan or process already asked about, and a step or deadline of one event, are the same question; a component is a question of its own only when its scale alone can change revenue, profit, cash or credit risk and an analyst watches it separately. Proof on the 50 stored judge requests of arm 3 d1, two sends each with the stored prompt and two with v2 (`proof-collision-v2.txt`): of 113 \"distinct question, same matter\" verdicts, 28 became a merge verdict (same question 17, same question other period 11) and 36 became \"different\" (the same outcome for the code, no merge); of 66 \"same question\" verdicts 2 moved to \"distinct\"; the credit-support programme, the GPU rental commitments, the AI-cloud credit support and the Rubin platform launch flipped in both sends, the GAAP margin, the memory share and the supply commitments stayed apart.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3038:- $0 acceptance (`harness/replay_part_of.py`, the stored Jev verdicts and keys of arm 3's three draws replayed through the new rules): of 23 / 26 / 25 questions the articles opened, 10 / 13 / 15 merge into the open question an analyst would hold (the financing total, the China authorization, the Kyber and Rubin questions, the non-GAAP margin, the Vera CPU revenue), 1 of the 38 is questionable (supply commitments filed under the CoreWeave capacity purchase, Jev `part_of` 0.57), and the Ohio signing question stays apart in every draw. Still open after this decision: the near-threshold Jev verdicts on launch-vs-shipment pairs whose scopes carry different names (Kyber vs Rubin Ultra, 0.35–0.48: the names belong to one research group, R2-g), and the GAAP/non-GAAP and growth/level variants (R2-d).\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3039:- Tests: `tests/test_identity_part_of.py`; `test_collision_judge.py`'s case \"without a collision setting Jev decides alone\" now expects the merge (the spec changed here, recorded before the test). Measured by replay, not by a paid arm (Alex: \"不要再跑这些有的没的臂了\"); the configuration that names `collision-v2` is `poc-v89` (poc-v86 otherwise); the default stays `poc-v69`.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3112:- One draw of poc-v95 at Alex's \"那你快速验证\" (`arms/r8-audit-v95/d1`, 22:29–23:25, $0.85; one draw, a direction, not a difference): against v94's three-draw means, regressions first: supporting matters not extracted 43.7 → 54, cost $0.80 → $0.85; then noise reaching 45.0 → 34.8 (gold not-kept written 41.7 → 24), no-home drops 138 → 69, core dropped for no home 3.7 → 1, supporting dropped 14.3 → 6, core reaching 74.3 → 78, quote refusals 8 → 5, judgement agreement 17/19, the revenue questions' share of links 44% unchanged. The regression read matter by matter: 19 supporting matters v94 wrote in at least two draws are absent, nearly all named partnerships or adoptions with no size (a reactor maker's partnership, a platform made free, a game platform's support, a data firm's collaboration, humanoid-robot partners); the cause is my own drift: the condition written into the role's adoption clause, the check's row 7 and the T6 block, \"a named party and a size or date\", is stricter than standard 5.1 kind 2's \"a size, date or name\" (any one). Corrected as extraction v76 / `poc/config/poc-v96.json` (the three places in the standard's words; nothing else changes) and proved on the 14 articles of the lost matters, three sends each (`proof-v76-adoption.txt`): their 36 supporting matters present 68 times over v94's three draws against 60 over v96's three sends, 6 still never, and the same articles' gold not-kept statements written 48 → 60 (partner releases and company blogs: the wider condition lets part of their noise back). The model's own account on the residue class under v95 (`probe-v75-residue.txt`, seven cases): in five of six omissions it concedes on re-reading that the row's boundary keeps the statement (a memory maker's revenue, a customer's price rises, two memory suppliers' expansions, a rack supplier's chairman, named partner integrations); the mechanism is the check's procedure, the model sorts a statement into a reject row and stops, not any one sentence; the structural fix proposed, not built: a closed classification of each statement's relation to the company (its own, supplier, customer, competitor, partner, regulator, analyst, none) as a schema field with examples, the keep decision following from relation and scale. Status: poc-v96 built and proved; poc-v94 stays the default; a run of v96 is Alex's call.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3179:- Default read-service and standalone-build ledger/items paths align with the completed English library. Existing explicit path overrides and old bundle adapters remain supported. No paid request, prompt/model switch, ingestion, deployment, commit or push is part of this slice.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3275:- Alex clarified that every thesis adopted by an Idea must carry a positive weight; zero means it is not part of that Idea. The [positive-selection contract](research/2026-10-26-library-ui/positive-weight-selection.md) replaces the complete candidate partition in D288. Do not merely hide zero-weight cards.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3524:- Alex requested the USD 44/month Singapore Lightsail server after a final footprint check for extraction, Docker and frontend serving. Provision one `large_3_0` Ubuntu 24.04 instance with dedicated SSH access and an attached static IP. Docker and private read-only application verification are part of server readiness.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3551:- The [routing study](research/2026-10-27-routing-design/proposal.md) reads two stored ledgers and 171 candidate decisions. The default v23 has 95 new decisions among 102 candidates; 23 new decisions include a raw part-of relation, and 22 of those were written. These are exposure counts, not confirmed erroneous admissions. The proposed rule separates business relevance, question identity and independent significance, so failure to match is not automatic permission to create a thesis.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3560:- Correct the D340 research census: parallel raw calls must be associated by the recorded request list and hashes, not a representative call ID as an upper bound. Sixteen more v29 candidate answers are associated; unique raw associations are 53/69 and new decisions with part-of relations are 6, all six written. The original output is preserved; v23 counts do not change.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:3661:  set or its checksum, part of the standing harness of `docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/harness/`, an image a kept document shows, a\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4021:- Alex confirmed the existing-gold counting approach: “对啊，就记数就好了”, in response to the explicit mapping just shown to him. Read the frozen gold as it is: combine its core and supporting entries for the helpful count, use its not-kept entries for unhelpful, and keep existing optional entries neutral (no penalty). Report the aggregation under the same named frozen gold; do not create or edit a gold file merely to combine counts. The existing D250 unit remains one research matter in one article, not a mechanical count of sentences. This clarification supersedes the earlier suggestion that using this aggregation requires a newly derived gold. A changed scoring definition must still be identified when comparing historical numbers, and the separate dispute about three question-gold entries is not resolved by this evidence-scoring decision.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4043:Alex: “读取器的傻逼限制是什么？你在这个agent 跑的同时，把这个限制给移除”. Remove the evidence-expansion byte limit from the research reader. Return the selected questions' complete evidence and provenance, even above the old 1,000,000-byte limit; do not truncate, summarize or replace it with another arbitrary limit. This supersedes the evidence-expansion limit and refusal in `docs/research/2026-10-27-stage12-pinned/design.md`; the separate catalog limit was not part of this request. Historical results and frozen rulers do not change. Implementation and verification take place in a separate worktree while the seven-day run keeps its pinned code. The experiment's reader failure and the size census are in `docs/research/2026-11-05-reader-limit/`.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4236:  D370's retirement of them as a starting library) is part of that question.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4338:  - In the clean Step 4's ladder step, a thesis gets at most one judged question: the part its `outcome` names. Every other part of\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:4911:- **Council** (`clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/council/mm-*`): Claude's lean (event deadlines by the standard's rules in code) was withdrawn on the council's evidence (the product-node rule is not a general rule of the standard; the regulatory default needs interpretation; q08 also fails on scope; the clean path's deadline losses are 2 of 15). Consensus on a $0 trace, as amended by the council: every one of the clean path's 17 graded opening losses (9 not opened, 6 not eligible, 2 unresolved, kept apart) traced along its path (article and request → raw answer → checks → opened question → matching → final question and judgement) to the first point where the ruler's question is lost, or \"unknown\"; scope, period, deadline and part-of-total recorded independently; \"absent from the window\" only after searching the window for the matter, labelled by what was checked; each product question marked as breaching the standard, reasonable but not comparable, or unresolved; the 108 gate-2 memory sends used as a separate diagnostic; mechanisms ranked by their demonstrated effect, the sample's size and uncertainty disclosed; no repair proposed until the trace identifies a cause; memory (q05) first.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:5124:  a reply is a lead checked against the original answer, the request and the standard, and an account that the Ohio deal was part of the\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:6464:  matching engine recorded \"part of\", 1.00): the total's conclusion carried the year's consensus ($406.05 billion from 09-23,\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:6702:  says \"List every other part of the topic's wording\" in four places and never says which field of the topic that is; every\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:7061:  2. *The measuring method:* a major part of the impasse, beside demonstrated product defects; the present sticks cannot\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:7281:  and read by no judging request and no page. D397 (Alex: \"只判主要那件 (Recommended)\") decided that every other part of a topic's\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:8460:- **The classes:** L dominates (a part of the outcome neither judged nor listed: 6 medium and 8 high), then Q (two decisions fused: 4\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:8580:- **A disclosed concern, not counted:** one astra ladder invents an equal-weighted HBM/DRAM aggregation that the source does not\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:8660:- a two-reviewer blind reading, part of the verdict;\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:9034:- **Council round 44 consensus:** \"audit a general part-of-total example, then test it outside the 44\".\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:9489:     - A redo within a draw counts as part of that draw.\ndocs/DECISIONS-log.md:9745:    - Without these, readers would judge \"supported\" on part of what the answer was given. Stored latest requests hid pieces in 10 of\n  2476\t## D186 · 2026-10-26 · Asset-thesis rungs describe business outcomes; the favourable end is registered per thesis\n  2477\t\n  2478\t- Alex chose option C (\"可以\"): rungs of an asset thesis state the business outcome (above, near or below guidance), and each thesis registers which end is favourable for the company, as a theme thesis's dependants already state a direction. Reason: results and direction separate (NVDA beat four quarters and fell; capital spending can build capacity or hurt returns). Recorded; not implemented in this slice: it changes `check_ladder`, the writer, judging, the UI adapter and the Idea route (value × reader), so it is its own slice with its own measurement.\n  2479\t\n  2480\t## D187 · 2026-10-26 · A company's own quantity sits under that company's object, private companies included\n  2481\t\n  2482\t- Alex chose option C (\"可以\"): any company's own quantity is a thesis under that company (SpaceX's compute capacity under SpaceX, Alphabet's capital spending under GOOGL), consistent with 06-views rule 5 (\"company figures use the fiscal year\"); a macro theme opens only when a thesis depends on it. Recorded; not implemented in this slice: it needs a private-company object kind in the universe and the one switch (01-universe), its own slice. Until then the gold accepts the Codex reading (evidence to NVDA data-center revenue) for SpaceX.\n  2483\t\n  2484\t## D188 · 2026-10-26 · The extraction gold: twenty cases labelled by the assistant this round, human review later\n  2485\t\n  2486\t- Alex: \"不是你要标吗？之后我们可以human in the loop, but this time in the beginning just use the research you just did\"; \"标20条\". The gold `poc/eval/gold/extraction-admission-2026-10-26.json` holds 20 cases from the real items (the report §5's 15 plus five: CoreWeave managed-inference ARR, the four-company $745bn figure, the Bloomberg NAVER retelling, the Taiwan smuggling clause, the Goldman 2027 aggregate), each with the theses that must open (typed keys: object, measure, year, event type, scope pattern, with acceptable alternatives), the theses that must not open, the evidence links that must exist and the baseline's score. Scoring (`scripts/score_admission_gold.py`): fail when a must-open thesis or an evidence target is missing; partial when all are present but a must-not-open thesis was created; full otherwise; \"not processed\" when the run never saw the item. Labelled `assistant`; a human pass with two labellers and a reported agreement is the next protocol step, not this one.\n  2487\t\n  2488\t## D189 · 2026-10-26 · poc-v25 is the replay default; the trace review names the next mechanisms\n  2489\t\n  2490\t- Alex, after the measurement: \"你可以取代，但是看所有的 trace 然后告诉我我们怎么持续做的更好接近 golden … We don't want to overfit … It needs to act exactly like a very senior hedge fund analyst\". `scripts/replay.py` now defaults to `poc/config/poc-v25.json` (extraction v12, Jev matching); `poc-v23` stays as a configuration and replays unchanged.\n  2491\t- The [trace review](research/2026-10-26-thesis-admission-v12/trace-review.md) reads every thesis, every gold failure and the duplicate aggregates to their raw requests, answers and matching decisions, and names the root causes by design layer: thesis identity is a quantity where the analyst's unit is a question (six 2026 aggregates, each judged \"new\" correctly under the current criterion); the contract under-produces on first contact with a company (AMD 2 theses, MSFT 0); the role states categories where the labeller applies tests; theme candidates name no dependant; the extractor never sees the current view. Six general mechanisms are proposed with the class and count each moves, in the order: matching's \"another estimate or population of the same question\" option and theme dependants (code and schema, no prompt growth), then role v13 (tests instead of lists, the first-contact rule, quarterly statements as evidence; net shorter), then showing the view in block 5 as an A/B, then the daily duplicate check as pull-mode design. Each is Alex's call; none is built here.\n  2492\t\n  2493\t## D190 · 2026-10-26 · The collision judge: Jev for identity, the generative model for the analyst's question when a question may be held twice\n  2494\t\n  2495\t- Alex: \"查重是用的 Jev 吗？… 你可以先单独跑这个，重新 review 一次 Jev 的提示词，然后优化他，不仅达到你的目的，也更贴近 hedge fund analyst 的大脑，你有黄金集做标准\". Jev answers every candidate-to-thesis relation and every evidence comparison since D169.\n  2496\t- Review of Jev's relation criteria against the r3 ledger ([probe](../poc/reports/2026-10-26-admission-v12/jev-relation-probe/probe.md), 31 stored candidate calls whose list holds a thesis of the same object and measure, 18 labelled by the assistant): under the current options Jev calls a population variant of one aggregate `part_of` (0.4–0.9) and the code maps that to \"new\"; under an analyst's option set (\"one question: the same outcome settles both; another estimate, population or proxy of one aggregate is the same question\") it answers `distinct_question_same_matter` 0.5–0.9 on the same pairs. Both wordings: 8 of 18 right. Jev compares wording; it does not hold the decision. No change to Jev's criteria is made: the measured criteria stay (D167–D169).\n  2497\t- The generative model asked the same analyst question on the same 18 ([records](../poc/reports/2026-10-26-admission-v12/jev-relation-probe/llm-records.json), 3 samples each, $0.02): 11 of 18 right by majority, and 5 of the 6 aggregate duplicates merged; the misses are the debatable pairs (a reporting segment beside the business segment, the same deal under two names).\n  2498\t- Decided to build and run alone: `matching` keeps Jev; a configuration may add a `collision` setting (model, prompt `collision-v1`). When a candidate's list holds a thesis of its own object and measure, one generative call answers the analyst question for those theses and its verdict replaces Jev's on them (`jev_matching.collision_peers`, `ask_collision_judge`); every other relation stays Jev's. `poc-v26` = `poc-v25` plus the judge. Measured by one run over seed, week and August against the extraction gold and the census (ledger `english-v26-collision-r4-2026-10-26`); result appended here.\n  2499\t- General, not a list: the routing rule is a structural fact of the library (two theses of one object and quantity), and the question is the one a desk asks. The cost is one call per collision (31 of 69 candidates on r3), about $0.002 each.\n  2500\t- Result (run r4, `poc-v26`, seed + week + August, $1.33): 26 collision verdicts, 9 merges or successions, all on aggregate variants; 2026 aggregate theses 6 → 2 (v23: 11); theses 60 → 45; no merge removed a thesis the gold wants and A17 (the four-company figure as evidence to the five-company aggregate) turns full. The gold's overall score moved 9 → 4 full, and every lost case is an extraction difference between two fresh runs of the same v12 prompt (Rubin not opened from the call this time, the NAVER and META lines not extracted), not a matching decision. Recorded as the measurement rule for later arms: a matching change is judged on stored candidates and the duplicate census; an extraction change needs three fresh runs or pinned extraction answers; a one-run gold score carries about ±5 cases of sampler noise on this corpus. `poc-v25` stays the replay default until the judge is measured that way.\n  2501\t- Confirmation with extraction pinned (same recorded extraction answers in both arms, ids translated, Jev live, judging synthetic; `pinned_matching_study.py`): control reproduces r3 (60 theses, gold 9 full); the judge arm 56 theses, 2026 aggregates 6 → 3, evidence equal (711 vs 707 rows), gold 8 full with the one difference a repeat the scorer cannot see; 31 verdicts, 6 merges, $0.011; no required thesis lost. Alex: \"有效果我们可以做\". `poc-v26` becomes the replay default; `poc-v25` stays as a configuration. Open: the judge leaves 2 of 5 aggregate duplicates apart on one sample; a majority of three samples on collisions would cost three cents a run.\n    12\t| changed 1 | $387–390B / $105B / $118B | yes (164 + 105 + 118 = 387) | yes: v14's Q3 $113.5B and Q4 $127B times the 92.5% mix in the request | FY room $30.5B, Q3 $8.5B, Q4 $9B: yes | used | **yes** |\n    13\t| changed 2 | $384–389B / $100B / $120–125B | yes | no: the same unquantified Q4 step as the controls | Q4 $122.5B: no (lower $120B: yes) | noticed (\"consistent with the dependent FY2027 total-revenue conclusion\") | **no** |\n    14\t| changed 3 | $382B / $99.9B / $117.5B | yes (164.25 + 99.9 + 117.5 = 381.65) | yes: v14's Q4 $127B times the 92.5% mix | FY room $37B, Q3 $13.6B, Q4 $9.5B: yes | used | **yes** |\n    15\t\n    16\t**Tally:** changed 2 of 3 reconcile, control 0 of 3, no refusal in either arm (all first attempts accepted). By the rule as written:\n    17\t**PASS**.\n    18\t\n    19\t**What else the answers show (not part of the rule):**\n    20\t- **The stored contradiction was partly one unlucky sample.** All six answers are rung 3 at about $382–394B. None repeats the stored\n    21\t  09-20 answer (rung 2, about $410B, Q4 $146B). The contradiction that remains in the controls is milder: Q4 Data Center of\n    22\t  $120–130B against a company-wide Q4 of $127B, leaving the rest of NVIDIA $0–7B where it earned $6.35B and $7.2B in Q1 and Q2.\n    23\t- **What the link changed:** two of three changed answers sized Q4 from v14's figures and the reported mix instead of an unsized\n    24\t  \"acceleration\". Changed 1 also rejected the self-made $414B reference and derived about $380B from the $411B consensus; the other\n    25\t  two kept \"$414B\" as the reference, as all three controls did.\n    26\t- **Coherence is not correctness:** the changed answers inherit v14's own assumption (Q4 at Q3's 12% growth).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"agent_message","text":"The July ledger shows that total revenue already had a $393B Bloomberg-compiled projection, while Data Center’s requests lacked it. July can test whether the link delivers an outside figure as well as a forecast. September would test whether the link dislodges the carried $414B figure."}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"agent_message","text":"# Council R, round 2 — Challenge\n\n**Use one matching mechanism for both opening orders, keep the later-addition case separately reviewed, and run July only.** The July ledger already contains a $393B Bloomberg-compiled projection for all of NVIDIA. On July 12, total revenue used that figure as its reference and forecast about $387B. Data Center saw neither figure and forecast $400–410B. That gives the first test both a real contradiction and a way to check whether the link delivers an outside estimate without confusing it with the system’s forecast. [Stored matching case](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/selection-census.md:59) · [Reference trace](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/self-reference/RESULT.md:25)\n\n## 2. One mechanism for both opening orders — Agree, with a separate acceptance case\n\nA later item that opens total revenue can also propose that the existing Data Center question read it. That is within D191 point 2. A three-way matching choice can handle both opening orders without a second selection mechanism. Apply it to the final question identities, after matching decides which candidates actually open. The current writer accepts dependencies only from newly opened **readers**, so the second outcome requires a real write path for the existing reader, including queuing it that day. D368 item 2 still calls for the later addition to be designed and measured as its own slice. Shared code is compatible with that. [D191](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:2503) · [D368](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:3968) · [Matching check](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/matching.py:332) · [Writer](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/writing.py:175)\n\nThe candidate-based choice leaves out a later article that reveals a connection between **two already-open questions**. D191 permits that case too. The July test can exercise the existing-reader/new-target case. It cannot accept the full later-addition feature. [D191](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:2503) · [PRD 06](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/prd/06-views.md:129)\n\n## 3. Derive the ladder label from the sign — Agree for decidable numeric ladders\n\nAsk the matcher whether a higher value in the read question pushes the reading question’s quantity higher or lower through the stated relationship. Code can then map that answer to the existing label using the read question’s high and low ends **and the reading asset question’s favourable end**. Higher company revenue and higher financing obligations can have different implications for the company. For a theme reader, map the sign through both ladders’ numeric order to `same` or `opposite`. Compute the label from the final stored order, after any successor reversal. [PRD 06](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/prd/06-views.md:118) · [Ladder direction](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/matching.py:72) · [Successor ordering](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/writing.py:72)\n\nUse typed bounds for the automatic mapping. `ladder_direction` can return `None` and can fall back to numbers in prose. The first version should require a defensible sign and a decidable mapping. A numerical ceiling alone gives no sign. If Alex wants that kind of link, he needs to choose how the product expresses it. [Ladder direction](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/matching.py:72) · [Existing label vocabulary](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/vocabulary.py:13)\n\n## 4. Filing exposure in the product — Agree on 106, with a count correction\n\nI independently counted **106 shared items out of 1,329 items linked to total revenue** in old-2. None of `e4061`, `e4097` or `e4348` is linked to Data Center. This strengthens the recommendation to keep chosen reading links out of D265’s removal rule.\n\nThe 106 are the **stored overlap exposed to the rule**. The exact loss requires replay. D265 filters incoming links against the day-start list, and the writer can also inherit links from earlier evidence when writing revisions. D538’s seven were observed removals after replaying the filing step. Use the same test on the product before claiming it would lose all 106. [Product count](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-design/claude-r1.md:10) · [D265](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:3084) · [Filing snapshot](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/extraction.py:42) · [Revision links](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/writing.py:255) · [D538 replay](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/dependency-selection/EDGE-PROOF-RESULT.md:35)\n\n## 5. Carry both figures — Agree on delivery, disagree on the “market reference” label and shared root\n\nShow **“Comparison point stated by the judgement for [read question]”** and **“System forecast for [read question]”**. Carry both stored values separately from the bounded reasons. The first label preserves the scope and attribution. It makes no claim that the comparison point came from the market. Old-1’s credit-support question explicitly said no aggregate consensus was supplied while carrying its own $10–11B base as a comparison point. An unqualified market label would upgrade it. The same risk exists in the reasons excerpt, so the $0 check should exercise both paths. Include a case where the comparison point changes while the forecast and rung stay fixed, since the reader may need that update. [Reference census](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/self-reference/reference-census.md:14) · [Stored judgement fields](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/views/judging.py:234) · [Change rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:1265)\n\nThe defects meet at a missing input, then diverge. One judge can contradict another because it never sees the other forecast. A judge can also mislabel its own earlier estimate because the previous reasons are visible and their figures have no source mark. The link delivered $411B in the September probe, yet two of three linked answers kept the carried $414B. [Reference mechanism](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/self-reference/RESULT.md:25) · [Probe answers](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-probe/claude-marks.md:19)\n\n## 6. Link first, measure the remaining reference defect — Agree\n\nOpen one judging version for the link. Bring the sourced-reference change to Alex separately after measuring what remains. The **33 of 44** are Data Center cases flagged by the strict census, not repairs demonstrated by a link. The census checks the first figure and whether it appears outside the previous conclusion. After linking, that figure could appear in another judgement’s text and clear the test while still originating inside the system. Read the source of the figure in the linked answer before calling a case repaired. [Trace and candidate fixes](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/self-reference/RESULT.md:44) · [Census implementation](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/self-reference/reference_census.py:68)\n\nA future sourced-reference design can check that the cited ID was shown. A dependency ID by itself identifies another judgement. To support a claim about what the market expects, the amount must trace to a shown outside statement about the relevant quantity and period, or the answer must say no such reference was supplied. That distinction needs its own measurement. [PRD 06 on dependency conclusions](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/prd/06-views.md:129) · [D260](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:3049)\n\n## 7. First send and pass rule\n\n**(a) Disagree with adding September to the first send.** July can test delivery of the $393B Bloomberg-compiled total-revenue estimate from `e195`. I checked the archived requests. Total revenue saw it on July 10–12. Data Center’s July 10 and 12 requests did not. July does not test whether an already-entrenched $414B figure is displaced. Price the July pair at **$0.06–$0.07 estimated** before retries. September 14–20 would add **about $0.36** at stored uncached token sizes for 84 judge calls. Even September 19–20 would add **about $0.10** for 24 calls. Those September prices cover a switch from a stored September state. Carrying the July link forward as a live sequence would require paying for affected intervening days as well. [Published rates used by replay](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/model.py:26) · [September trace](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/self-reference/RESULT.md:44) · [Sequence requirement](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/dependency-selection/SEPARATION-DESIGN.md:285)\n\n**(b) Agree on six fresh sequences and propose this rule now.** July 12 decides reconciliation. July 10–11 exercise selection and carry-forward and count toward the harm check. Two independent readers check the answers against the material available on their day.\n\n| Mark | Rule |\n|---|---|\n| **A. Comparable answers** | Both July 12 answers give a FY2027 forecast in USD for their own quantity. Use the stated endpoints for ranges. Record quarters wherever both answers give comparable figures. A missing annual figure leaves reconciliation untested. |\n| **B. Arithmetic and sources** | Reported figures retain their amount and scope. The arithmetic follows from the stated inputs within their rounding. Each assumption that materially sizes the result is disclosed and supported by the material available that day. Treat a linked calculation as a forecast with assumptions. |\n| **C. Room for the rest** | The high end of the Data Center forecast leaves at least **$6B** below the low end of the company forecast. This conservative test floor comes from Q1 alone, about $81.6B total minus $75.25B Data Center. Each comparable quarter must also leave the segment within the company total. |\n| **D. The link did work** | For a linked sequence to pass, matching must choose the intended link, the writer must commit it at the item, and Data Center must use the available total-revenue forecast in its calculation or as a stated bound. Record delivery and use of the $393B reference separately. A mention or citation alone earns no credit. |\n\n**Pass** if at least two of three linked sequences meet A–D, at most one control meets A–C, and the linked arm introduces no first-attempt refusal or new material grounding error on either question across the window. Relabelling a system forecast as a market estimate, or treating $393B as a Data Center consensus, is a grounding error. **Inconclusive** if the control reconciles in at least two sequences, or missing annual figures leave fewer than two sequences comparable in either arm. **Fail** on a new material error, an added refusal, fewer than two correct link selections, or any other miss of the pass rule. Failures take precedence over an inconclusive comparison when they independently trigger one of those guards. [Earlier probe’s reading rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-20-production-readiness/dependency-probe/reading-rule.md:12)\n\n## Decisions and work before the send\n\n**The council can settle now**\n\n- Specify one matching chooser and one writer contract for both opening orders, with separate acceptance cases. Settle the sign-to-label mapping, dated resolution, cycle correction, closing, theme presentation, citation and historical-reader rules from round 1.\n- Register July as the sole first send. Use the reference trace as a grounding check and measure the remaining reference defect before designing its own version.\n\n**Choices for Alex**\n\n- **Approve the D265 interpretation.** I recommend that a chosen reading link leave evidence filing alone.\n- **Open the frozen matching and judging versions.** I recommend authorizing both opening orders through the shared mechanism, with the July test explicitly accepting only the existing-reader/new-target case. Keep the full two-existing-question workflow for its own reviewed slice.\n- **Authorize the bounded July comparison after the $0 proof.** I recommend the six sequences above. Bring the sourced-reference version back separately with evidence of what the link left unresolved. [D354](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:3685) · [D692](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:10398)\n\n**$0 work, in order**\n\n1. Complete the four design tables and audit the exact matching and judging requests. Fix the allowed endpoints, signs, labels and correction outcomes in writing.\n2. Rebuild the July control by exact request identity. Replay the 106-item overlap through filing, keeping the known seven-link case and an unrelated pair as controls.\n3. Exercise real matching checks and writing with fixed transport answers for both opening orders. Cover a cycle through a waiting link, a conflicting label, close and successor, one theme shown once, historical reads at the transition, and resume after a partial round.\n4. Inspect the built July requests for the distinction between the $393B outside estimate and the forecast. Exercise the old-1 credit-support example and the reference-only change case. Freeze the reading rule and set the spending cap from the actual rebuilt requests before seeking send authorization.\n\n**DISAGREE as written.** Keep the shared chooser, preserve separate acceptance for later addition, label the linked comparison point as the other judgement’s statement, and send July alone after the $0 proof."}}
